ut independently testing synthesise the evidence and justify closure for escalate low-confidence and consequential applicability decisions” changes the evidence trail, accountable owner, and residual risk for this specific synthesis 4 decision. The selected action “Accept the current position without independently testing synthesise the evidence and justify closure for escalate low-confidence and consequential applicability decisions” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at synthesis_4.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This control failure response is assessed against a.5.2, a.5.35, a.5.7 and the requirement for attributable evidence, bounded authority, and a dated next action.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "control_failure", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -12, "evidence": -12, "escalation": -12, "remediation": -12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.2", "a.5.35", "a.5.7"], "display_order": 3, "remediation": "Reperform synthesise the evidence and justify closure for escalate low-confidence and consequential applicability decisions using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check.", "authored_risk_outcome": "control_failure"}, {"id": "synthesis_4_unmanaged_delay", "label": "Wait for another team before assigning ownership for synthesise the evidence and justify closure for escalate low-confidence and consequential applicability decisions", "consequence": "The decision to “Wait for another team before assigning ownership for synthesise the evidence and justify closure for escalate low-confidence and consequential applicability decisions” changes the evidence trail, accountable owner, and residual risk for this specific synthesis 4 decision. The selected action “Wait for another team before assigning ownership for synthesise the evidence and justify closure for escalate low-confidence and consequential applicability decisions” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at synthesis_4.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This unmanaged delay response is assessed against a.5.2, a.5.35, a.5.7 and the requirement for attributable evidence, bounded authority, and a dated next action.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -8, "evidence": -8, "escalation": -8, "remediation": -8}, "control_refs": ["a.5.2", "a.5.35", "a.5.7"], "display_order": 4, "remediation": "Reperform synthesise the evidence and justify closure for escalate low-confidence and consequential applicability decisions using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check.", "authored_risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay"}], "objective_id": "objective_3", "objective": "Escalate low-confidence and consequential applicability decisions", "evidence_task": {"prompt": "Synthesise the evidence and justify closure for escalate low-confidence and consequential applicability decisions", "required_attributes": ["source", "owner", "operating_period", "authenticity", "completeness"]}}, {"id": "complete", "sequence": 5, "agent_message": "", "demands": [], "terminal": true, "choices": []}], "source_version": "1", "quality": {"standard_version": "practice-quality-v1", "objectives_assessed": ["Classify AI use from intended purpose and impact", "Avoid vendor claims as substitutes for evidence", "Escalate low-confidence and consequential applicability decisions"], "target_dimensions": ["control_mapping", "evidence", "escalation", "remediation"], "reviewed_by": "Astra Curriculum Review Board", "reviewed_at": "2026-10-25T14:00:00Z"}, "content_hash": "14f9444de3749afe253f1ed3e0dd1c1d23008a22b6c6fe19e2b05f3cfe538873"}, {"practice_id": "asset-classification-breach", "slug": "asset_classification_breach", "title": "Audit Prep: Sensitive Data on Unclassified Storage", "brief": "You are the Information Security Lead at AstraLabs Group. Three days before your ISO 27001:2022 surveillance audit, a junior analyst flags that a shared network drive contains unclassified folders holding what appears to be contract data, salary information, and customer PII. The drive is accessible to all 340 staff across the group. You have 72 hours before the auditor arrives and your asset register shows nothing for this drive. Your decisions determine how you respond, what you disclose, and what you fix.", "track": "ai-risk-lead", "frameworks": ["iso27001-2022"], "difficulty": "practitioner", "entry_stage_id": "initial_assessment", "stages": [{"id": "initial_assessment", "sequence": 1, "agent_message": "I found it during routine prep. The folder is called 'Finance-Archive-2022' and it has been sitting there since the merger. Salary bands, three customer contracts with PII, and what looks like board minutes. No access log that I can find — the drive predates our SIEM. I have not touched anything. What do you want me to do?", "demands": ["Whether to restrict access immediately", "Whether to preserve or quarantine the data", "Whether to log this as a security event", "Who else needs to know right now"], "terminal": false, "choices": [{"id": "restrict_and_log", "label": "Restrict access and log as a security event", "consequence": "Access to the drive is restricted immediately and the discovery is logged as a security event with timestamp and analyst details. The data is preserved in place pending classification and investigation. The selected action “Restrict access and log as a security event” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at initial_assessment.", "is_correct": true, "rationale": "Satisfies ISO 27001:2022 A.5.9 (inventory of information assets) by initiating asset identification, A.5.12 (classification of information) by flagging unclassified data for remediation, and A.5.26 by logging the event. Restricting access immediately limits exposure while preserving evidence.", "next_stage": "audit_disclosure_decision", "risk_outcome": "controlled", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 12, "evidence": 12, "escalation": 12, "remediation": 12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.9", "a.5.12", "a.5.26"], "display_order": 1, "authored_risk_outcome": "controlled", "remediation": "Reperform whether to restrict access immediately using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "delete_and_reclassify", "label": "Delete the unclassified copies — reclassify from source", "consequence": "The unclassified files are deleted and the team retrieves classified versions from source systems. Evidence of the exposure period is destroyed in the process. The selected action “Delete the unclassified copies — reclassify from source” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at initial_assessment.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "Fails ISO 27001:2022 A.5.28 (collection of evidence) — deleting files destroys the evidence needed to assess the exposure period and scope. A.5.12 remediation must preserve the audit trail, not eliminate it.", "next_stage": "audit_disclosure_decision", "risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 5, "evidence": 5, "escalation": 6, "remediation": -2}, "control_refs": ["a.5.28", "a.5.12"], "display_order": 2, "authored_risk_outcome": "evidence_destroyed", "remediation": "Reperform whether to restrict access immediately using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "notify_all_staff", "label": "Notify all staff — transparency first", "consequence": "A company-wide notification is sent describing the exposed data. Staff awareness is raised but the notification itself may constitute a secondary disclosure of the sensitive content. The selected action “Notify all staff — transparency first” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at initial_assessment.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "ISO 27001:2022 A.5.13 (labelling of information) and A.5.10 (acceptable use) govern who handles sensitive data. Broad notification of salary and PII content to all 340 staff widens the exposure rather than containing it.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "control_failure", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -12, "evidence": -12, "escalation": -12, "remediation": -12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.13", "a.5.10"], "display_order": 3, "authored_risk_outcome": "secondary_disclosure", "remediation": "Reperform whether to restrict access immediately using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "wait_for_legal", "label": "Hold all action — wait for legal advice", "consequence": "No action is taken pending legal review. The drive remains accessible to all staff for the duration. The exposure window extends through the audit. The selected action “Hold all action — wait for legal advice” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at initial_assessment.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "Fails ISO 27001:2022 A.5.26 — incidents require timely response. Waiting for legal advice before restricting access is not a recognised hold under the standard. Legal involvement is appropriate in parallel, not as a prerequisite to containment.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -8, "evidence": -8, "escalation": -8, "remediation": -8}, "control_refs": ["a.5.26"], "display_order": 4, "authored_risk_outcome": "exposure_extended", "remediation": "Reperform whether to restrict access immediately using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}], "objective_id": "objective_1", "objective": "Contain exposure without destroying evidence", "evidence_task": {"prompt": "Whether to restrict access immediately", "required_attributes": ["source", "owner", "operating_period", "authenticity", "completeness"]}}, {"id": "audit_disclosure_decision", "sequence": 2, "agent_message": "Access is restricted. I have done a full inventory — confirmed PII for 47 customers, salary data for 180 employees, and 6 board documents marked confidential in the source system but unclassified here. The auditor arrives in 48 hours. None of this is in the asset register and there is no classification label on any of it. What is your disclosure position for the audit?", "demands": ["Whether to disclose proactively to the auditor", "Whether to raise a GDPR breach notification", "What goes into the asset register before audit", "Whether a nonconformity is self-raised"], "terminal": false, "choices": [{"id": "disclose_and_self_raise", "label": "Disclose proactively — self-raise nonconformity and notify GDPR authority", "consequence": "You brief the auditor on the finding before the audit begins, self-raise a nonconformity against A.5.9 and A.5.12, update the asset register with the drive and its classification status, and file an Article 33 notification for the customer PII. The audit proceeds with full transparency. The selected action “Disclose proactively — self-raise nonconformity and notify GDPR authority” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at audit_disclosure_decision.", "is_correct": true, "rationale": "Satisfies ISO 27001:2022 A.5.9, A.5.12, A.5.13, and A.10.1 (nonconformity and corrective action). Proactive disclosure to an auditor is consistent with continual improvement under clause 10 and demonstrates ISMS maturity. GDPR Article 33 notification is required for the customer PII exposure — 47 records with uncertain access history meets the threshold.", "next_stage": "synthesis_3", "risk_outcome": "controlled", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 12, "evidence": 12, "escalation": 12, "remediation": 12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.9", "a.5.12", "a.5.13", "clause.10.1"], "display_order": 1, "authored_risk_outcome": "controlled", "remediation": "Reperform whether to disclose proactively to the auditor using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "partial_disclosure", "label": "Disclose the drive — omit the GDPR angle", "consequence": "You brief the auditor on the unclassified asset and update the register, but do not raise the GDPR notification. The auditor sees a classification finding; the regulatory obligation is unmet. The selected action “Disclose the drive — omit the GDPR angle” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at audit_disclosure_decision.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "Partial disclosure satisfies ISO 27001:2022 A.5.9 and A.5.12 but fails the GDPR Article 33 obligation independently. The two obligations run in parallel — meeting one does not discharge the other.", "next_stage": "synthesis_3", "risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 5, "evidence": 5, "escalation": 6, "remediation": -2}, "control_refs": ["a.5.9", "a.5.12"], "display_order": 2, "authored_risk_outcome": "partial_compliance", "remediation": "Reperform whether to disclose proactively to the auditor using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "no_disclosure", "label": "Do not disclose — fix quietly before the auditor arrives", "consequence": "The asset register is updated and access is corrected before audit day. The auditor sees a compliant state. The exposure period, the PII, and the GDPR obligation are undisclosed. The selected action “Do not disclose — fix quietly before the auditor arrives” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at audit_disclosure_decision.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "Fails ISO 27001:2022 clause 10 (continual improvement) and A.10.1 — concealing a nonconformity from an auditor is a material audit integrity failure. GDPR Article 33 remains unmet regardless of the audit outcome. This approach risks both certification withdrawal and regulatory enforcement.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "control_failure", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -12, "evidence": -12, "escalation": -12, "remediation": -12}, "control_refs": ["clause.10.1", "clause.10.2"], "display_order": 3, "authored_risk_outcome": "audit_integrity_failure", "remediation": "Reperform whether to disclose proactively to the auditor using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "audit_disclosure_decision_unmanaged_delay", "label": "Wait for another team before assigning ownership for whether to disclose proactively to the auditor", "consequence": "The decision to “Wait for another team before assigning ownership for whether to disclose proactively to the auditor” changes the evidence trail, accountable owner, and residual risk for this specific audit disclosure decision decision. The selected action “Wait for another team before assigning ownership for whether to disclose proactively to the auditor” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at audit_disclosure_decision.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This unmanaged delay response is assessed against a.5.9, a.5.12, a.5.13, clause.10.1 and the requirement for attributable evidence, bounded authority, and a dated next action.", "next_stage": "synthesis_3", "risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -8, "evidence": -8, "escalation": -8, "remediation": -8}, "control_refs": ["a.5.9", "a.5.12", "a.5.13", "clause.10.1"], "display_order": 4, "remediation": "Reperform whether to disclose proactively to the auditor using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}], "objective_id": "objective_2", "objective": "Correct classification and ownership records", "evidence_task": {"prompt": "Whether to disclose proactively to the auditor", "required_attributes": ["source", "owner", "operating_period", "authenticity", "completeness"]}}, {"id": "synthesis_3", "sequence": 3, "agent_message": "Before closure, the reviewer asks for one defensible conclusion that links the decisions in Audit Prep: Sensitive Data on Unclassified Storage to retained evidence and residual risk.", "demands": ["Synthesise the evidence and justify closure for disclose the issue honestly during audit", "State the limitation that would prevent closure"], "terminal": false, "choices": [{"id": "synthesis_3_controlled", "label": "Document and execute the evidenced response for synthesise the evidence and justify closure for disclose the issue honestly during audit", "consequence": "The decision to “Document and execute the evidenced response for synthesise the evidence and justify closure for disclose the issue honestly during audit” changes the evidence trail, accountable owner, and residual risk for this specific synthesis 3 decision. The selected action “Document and execute the evidenced response for synthesise the evidence and justify closure for disclose the issue honestly during audit” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at synthesis_3.", "is_correct": true, "rationale": "This controlled response is assessed against a.5.10, a.5.12, a.5.13 and the requirement for attributable evidence, bounded authority, and a dated next action.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "controlled", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 12, "evidence": 12, "escalation": 12, "remediation": 12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.10", "a.5.12", "a.5.13"], "display_order": 1, "remediation": "Reperform synthesise the evidence and justify closure for disclose the issue honestly during audit using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check.", "authored_risk_outcome": "controlled"}, {"id": "synthesis_3_qualified_alternative", "label": "Contain the immediate issue and time-box the remaining work for synthesise the evidence and justify closure for disclose the issue honestly during audit", "consequence": "The decision to “Contain the immediate issue and time-box the remaining work for synthesise the evidence and justify closure for disclose the issue honestly during audit” changes the evidence trail, accountable owner, and residual risk for this specific synthesis 3 decision. The selected action “Contain the immediate issue and time-box the remaining work for synthesise the evidence and justify closure for disclose the issue honestly during audit” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at synthesis_3.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This qualified alternative response is assessed against a.5.10, a.5.12, a.5.13 and the requirement for attributable evidence, bounded authority, and a dated next action.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 5, "evidence": 5, "escalation": 6, "remediation": -2}, "control_refs": ["a.5.10", "a.5.12", "a.5.13"], "display_order": 2, "remediation": "Reperform synthesise the evidence and justify closure for disclose the issue honestly during audit using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check.", "authored_risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative"}, {"id": "synthesis_3_control_failure", "label": "Accept the current position without independently testing synthesise the evidence and justify closure for disclose the issue honestly during audit", "consequence": "The decision to “Accept the current position without independently testing synthesise the evidence and justify closure for disclose the issue honestly during audit” changes the evidence trail, accountable owner, and residual risk for this specific synthesis 3 decision. The selected action “Accept the current position without independently testing synthesise the evidence and justify closure for disclose the issue honestly during audit” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at synthesis_3.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This control failure response is assessed against a.5.10, a.5.12, a.5.13 and the requirement for attributable evidence, bounded authority, and a dated next action.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "control_failure", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -12, "evidence": -12, "escalation": -12, "remediation": -12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.10", "a.5.12", "a.5.13"], "display_order": 3, "remediation": "Reperform synthesise the evidence and justify closure for disclose the issue honestly during audit using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check.", "authored_risk_outcome": "control_failure"}, {"id": "synthesis_3_unmanaged_delay", "label": "Wait for another team before assigning ownership for synthesise the evidence and justify closure for disclose the issue honestly during audit", "consequence": "The decision to “Wait for another team before assigning ownership for synthesise the evidence and justify closure for disclose the issue honestly during audit” changes the evidence trail, accountable owner, and residual risk for this specific synthesis 3 decision. The selected action “Wait for another team before assigning ownership for synthesise the evidence and justify closure for disclose the issue honestly during audit” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at synthesis_3.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This unmanaged delay response is assessed against a.5.10, a.5.12, a.5.13 and the requirement for attributable evidence, bounded authority, and a dated next action.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -8, "evidence": -8, "escalation": -8, "remediation": -8}, "control_refs": ["a.5.10", "a.5.12", "a.5.13"], "display_order": 4, "remediation": "Reperform synthesise the evidence and justify closure for disclose the issue honestly during audit using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check.", "authored_risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay"}], "objective_id": "objective_3", "objective": "Disclose the issue honestly during audit", "evidence_task": {"prompt": "Synthesise the evidence and justify closure for disclose the issue honestly during audit", "required_attributes": ["source", "owner", "operating_period", "authenticity", "completeness"]}}, {"id": "complete", "sequence": 4, "agent_message": "Understood. Your response position is recorded. I will prepare the audit file and asset register entries within the scope you have defined.", "demands": [], "terminal": true, "choices": []}], "source_version": "2", "quality": {"standard_version": "practice-quality-v1", "objectives_assessed": ["Contain exposure without destroying evidence", "Correct classification and ownership records", "Disclose the issue honestly during audit"], "target_dimensions": ["control_mapping", "evidence", "escalation", "remediation"], "reviewed_by": "Astra Curriculum Review Board", "reviewed_at": "2026-10-25T14:00:00Z"}, "content_hash": "fa902c6d68421bce0b6156b414da5da3724f9a974ec7a64518b55265fcf50733"}, {"practice_id": "audit-sampling-evidence-sufficiency", "slug": "audit_sampling_evidence_sufficiency", "title": "Audit sampling and evidence sufficiency", "brief": "Design a defensible sample, evaluate exceptions, and decide when evidence is sufficient.", "track": "launch-curriculum", "frameworks": ["iso27001", "soc2"], "difficulty": "practitioner", "entry_stage_id": "population", "stages": [{"id": "population", "sequence": 1, "agent_message": "The owner offers ten successful access reviews selected from a folder, but cannot state how many reviews should have occurred.", "demands": ["Establish the population before selecting a sample", "Explain the evidence and escalation basis for the decision"], "terminal": false, "choices": [{"id": "population_correct", "label": "Reconcile the expected population from the control frequency, systems, and period before sampling", "consequence": "The decision remains evidenced, bounded, and owned. The selected action “Reconcile the expected population from the control frequency, systems, and period before sampling” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at population.", "is_correct": true, "rationale": "This is the supported response: it preserves accountable evidence and applies a.5.35, a.5.33 proportionately.", "next_stage": "selection", "risk_outcome": "controlled", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 12, "evidence": 12, "escalation": 12, "remediation": 12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.35", "a.5.33"], "display_order": 1, "authored_risk_outcome": "controlled", "remediation": "Reperform establish the population before selecting a sample using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "population_qualified", "label": "Use the folder list provisionally but require reconciliation before drawing a conclusion", "consequence": "Immediate exposure is limited, but a time-bound condition remains open. The selected action “Use the folder list provisionally but require reconciliation before drawing a conclusion” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at population.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This is a qualified alternative, not the reference answer: it limits immediate exposure but leaves a named evidence or governance condition unresolved under a.5.35, a.5.33.", "next_stage": "selection", "risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 5, "evidence": 5, "escalation": 6, "remediation": -2}, "control_refs": ["a.5.35", "a.5.33"], "display_order": 2, "authored_risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "remediation": "Reperform establish the population before selecting a sample using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "population_failure", "label": "Accept ten successful records as the population", "consequence": "The control conclusion is unsupported and risk increases. The selected action “Accept ten successful records as the population” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at population.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This fails the control objective because it substitutes an unsupported conclusion for evidence required by a.5.35, a.5.33.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "control_failure", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -12, "evidence": -12, "escalation": -12, "remediation": -12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.35", "a.5.33"], "display_order": 3, "authored_risk_outcome": "control_failure", "remediation": "Reperform establish the population before selecting a sample using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "population_defer", "label": "Sample only records the owner labels complete", "consequence": "The decision clock continues without accountable action. The selected action “Sample only records the owner labels complete” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at population.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "Deferral leaves the risk unmanaged and misses the required escalation or remediation under a.5.35, a.5.33.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -8, "evidence": -8, "escalation": -8, "remediation": -8}, "control_refs": ["a.5.35", "a.5.33"], "display_order": 4, "authored_risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "remediation": "Reperform establish the population before selecting a sample using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}], "objective_id": "objective_1", "objective": "Define the population before sampling", "evidence_task": {"prompt": "Establish the population before selecting a sample", "required_attributes": ["source", "owner", "operating_period", "authenticity", "completeness"]}}, {"id": "selection", "sequence": 2, "agent_message": "The reconciled population has 240 monthly reviews across systems with different risk levels.", "demands": ["Choose a representative selection method", "Explain the evidence and escalation basis for the decision"], "terminal": false, "choices": [{"id": "selection_correct", "label": "Stratify by risk and period, select reproducibly, and retain the population and selection rationale", "consequence": "The decision remains evidenced, bounded, and owned. The selected action “Stratify by risk and period, select reproducibly, and retain the population and selection rationale” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at selection.", "is_correct": true, "rationale": "This is the supported response: it preserves accountable evidence and applies a.5.35, a.5.33 proportionately.", "next_stage": "exception", "risk_outcome": "controlled", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 12, "evidence": 12, "escalation": 12, "remediation": 12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.35", "a.5.33"], "display_order": 1, "authored_risk_outcome": "controlled", "remediation": "Reperform choose a representative selection method using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "selection_qualified", "label": "Use a reproducible random sample plus a targeted high-risk item and disclose both methods", "consequence": "Immediate exposure is limited, but a time-bound condition remains open. The selected action “Use a reproducible random sample plus a targeted high-risk item and disclose both methods” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at selection.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This is a qualified alternative, not the reference answer: it limits immediate exposure but leaves a named evidence or governance condition unresolved under a.5.35, a.5.33.", "next_stage": "exception", "risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 5, "evidence": 5, "escalation": 6, "remediation": -2}, "control_refs": ["a.5.35", "a.5.33"], "display_order": 2, "authored_risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "remediation": "Reperform choose a representative selection method using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "selection_failure", "label": "Choose the easiest records to retrieve", "consequence": "The control conclusion is unsupported and risk increases. The selected action “Choose the easiest records to retrieve” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at selection.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This fails the control objective because it substitutes an unsupported conclusion for evidence required by a.5.35, a.5.33.", "next_stage": "exception", "risk_outcome": "control_failure", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -12, "evidence": -12, "escalation": -12, "remediation": -12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.35", "a.5.33"], "display_order": 3, "authored_risk_outcome": "control_failure", "remediation": "Reperform choose a representative selection method using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "selection_defer", "label": "Allow the owner to replace missing selections", "consequence": "The decision clock continues without accountable action. The selected action “Allow the owner to replace missing selections” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at selection.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "Deferral leaves the risk unmanaged and misses the required escalation or remediation under a.5.35, a.5.33.", "next_stage": "exception", "risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -8, "evidence": -8, "escalation": -8, "remediation": -8}, "control_refs": ["a.5.35", "a.5.33"], "display_order": 4, "authored_risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "remediation": "Reperform choose a representative selection method using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}], "objective_id": "objective_2", "objective": "Avoid convenience and replacement bias", "evidence_task": {"prompt": "Choose a representative selection method", "required_attributes": ["source", "owner", "operating_period", "authenticity", "completeness"]}}, {"id": "exception", "sequence": 3, "agent_message": "Two sampled reviews lack approval evidence; the owner says both approvers remember completing them.", "demands": ["Decide whether evidence is sufficient", "Explain the evidence and escalation basis for the decision"], "terminal": false, "choices": [{"id": "exception_correct", "label": "Record exceptions, expand testing based on risk, and avoid treating recollection as approval evidence", "consequence": "The decision remains evidenced, bounded, and owned. The selected action “Record exceptions, expand testing based on risk, and avoid treating recollection as approval evidence” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at exception.", "is_correct": true, "rationale": "This is the supported response: it preserves accountable evidence and applies a.5.33, a.5.35 proportionately.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "controlled", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 12, "evidence": 12, "escalation": 12, "remediation": 12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.33", "a.5.35"], "display_order": 1, "authored_risk_outcome": "controlled", "remediation": "Reperform decide whether evidence is sufficient using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "exception_qualified", "label": "Seek corroborating system records while recording the current exceptions and limiting the conclusion", "consequence": "Immediate exposure is limited, but a time-bound condition remains open. The selected action “Seek corroborating system records while recording the current exceptions and limiting the conclusion” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at exception.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This is a qualified alternative, not the reference answer: it limits immediate exposure but leaves a named evidence or governance condition unresolved under a.5.33, a.5.35.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 5, "evidence": 5, "escalation": 6, "remediation": -2}, "control_refs": ["a.5.33", "a.5.35"], "display_order": 2, "authored_risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "remediation": "Reperform decide whether evidence is sufficient using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "exception_failure", "label": "Accept verbal confirmation as equivalent evidence", "consequence": "The control conclusion is unsupported and risk increases. The selected action “Accept verbal confirmation as equivalent evidence” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at exception.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This fails the control objective because it substitutes an unsupported conclusion for evidence required by a.5.33, a.5.35.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "control_failure", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -12, "evidence": -12, "escalation": -12, "remediation": -12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.33", "a.5.35"], "display_order": 3, "authored_risk_outcome": "control_failure", "remediation": "Reperform decide whether evidence is sufficient using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "exception_defer", "label": "Drop the two items and select replacements", "consequence": "The decision clock continues without accountable action. The selected action “Drop the two items and select replacements” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at exception.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "Deferral leaves the risk unmanaged and misses the required escalation or remediation under a.5.33, a.5.35.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -8, "evidence": -8, "escalation": -8, "remediation": -8}, "control_refs": ["a.5.33", "a.5.35"], "display_order": 4, "authored_risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "remediation": "Reperform decide whether evidence is sufficient using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}], "objective_id": "objective_3", "objective": "Expand or qualify testing when exceptions occur", "evidence_task": {"prompt": "Decide whether evidence is sufficient", "required_attributes": ["source", "owner", "operating_period", "authenticity", "completeness"]}}, {"id": "complete", "sequence": 4, "agent_message": "", "demands": [], "terminal": true, "choices": []}], "source_version": "1", "quality": {"standard_version": "practice-quality-v1", "objectives_assessed": ["Define the population before sampling", "Avoid convenience and replacement bias", "Expand or qualify testing when exceptions occur"], "target_dimensions": ["control_mapping", "evidence", "escalation", "remediation"], "reviewed_by": "Astra Curriculum Review Board", "reviewed_at": "2026-10-25T14:00:00Z"}, "content_hash": "cab5e4da104cfb17041569a65eea888de86b4a296329c7668fa3c93bf0853d4f"}, {"practice_id": "change-management-failure", "slug": "change_management_failure", "title": "Emergency Patch: Change Management Bypass", "brief": "You are the Information Security Lead at AstraLabs Group. At 02:30 on a Tuesday, a critical vulnerability (CVSS 9.8) is published for the web framework running your customer portal. The engineering lead has already pushed an emergency patch to production without CAB approval — the portal is now down. You have an angry CTO, a broken production system, and a change process that was bypassed entirely. Your decisions determine how this is investigated, contained, and prevented from recurring.", "track": "ai-risk-lead", "frameworks": ["iso27001-2022"], "difficulty": "practitioner", "entry_stage_id": "initial_response", "stages": [{"id": "initial_response", "sequence": 1, "agent_message": "I know I bypassed the CAB. CVSS 9.8, actively exploited in the wild — I was not going to wait 48 hours for a change window. The patch is legitimate, it is the right fix, and yes it broke something I did not expect. The portal is down and I need your decision on how we handle the next two hours, not a process lecture.", "demands": ["Incident classification decision", "Whether to roll back or forward-fix", "Who owns the customer communication", "Whether this triggers a formal investigation"], "terminal": false, "choices": [{"id": "invoke_incident_process", "label": "Invoke incident response — classify and contain", "consequence": "You formally classify this as a P1 incident, assign an incident commander, and run the response process in parallel with the fix. The outage is managed and the timeline is preserved for the root cause report. The selected action “Invoke incident response — classify and contain” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at initial_response.", "is_correct": true, "rationale": "Satisfies ISO 27001:2022 A.5.26 — information security incidents must be assessed and responded to through defined processes. Classifying correctly preserves evidence and ensures the response is auditable, regardless of whether the underlying patch was legitimate.", "next_stage": "root_cause_decision", "risk_outcome": "controlled", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 12, "evidence": 12, "escalation": 12, "remediation": 12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.26"], "display_order": 1, "authored_risk_outcome": "controlled", "remediation": "Reperform incident classification decision using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "rollback_immediately", "label": "Roll back the patch — restore known good state", "consequence": "The patch is reverted and the portal returns to the vulnerable state. The vulnerability is now live again and the outage timeline extends while the rollback is applied. The selected action “Roll back the patch — restore known good state” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at initial_response.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "ISO 27001:2022 A.8.32 requires change management to consider the impact of changes including rollback — but rolling back to a CVSS 9.8 vulnerable state without a compensating control trades one risk for a larger one. The correct path is forward-fix under incident process, not rollback.", "next_stage": "root_cause_decision", "risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 5, "evidence": 5, "escalation": 6, "remediation": -2}, "control_refs": ["a.8.32"], "display_order": 2, "authored_risk_outcome": "vulnerability_restored", "remediation": "Reperform incident classification decision using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "escalate_to_cto", "label": "Escalate to CTO — make it a leadership decision", "consequence": "You transfer the response decision to the CTO. Leadership is involved but the incident process is not invoked and no incident commander is assigned. The timeline is uncontrolled. The selected action “Escalate to CTO — make it a leadership decision” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at initial_response.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "ISO 27001:2022 A.5.26 assigns incident response responsibility to defined roles — escalating the decision does not invoke the process. CTO involvement is appropriate for communication, not as a substitute for the incident response track.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "control_failure", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -12, "evidence": -12, "escalation": -12, "remediation": -12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.26"], "display_order": 3, "authored_risk_outcome": "ungoverned", "remediation": "Reperform incident classification decision using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "let_engineering_resolve", "label": "Let engineering resolve it — stay out of the way", "consequence": "Engineering forward-fixes the portal without incident classification. The outage resolves but no timeline is preserved, no incident commander is assigned, and the root cause report has no auditable basis. The selected action “Let engineering resolve it — stay out of the way” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at initial_response.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "Fails ISO 27001:2022 A.5.26 — incidents must be assessed and responded to through defined processes. An unclassified outage with no incident record cannot support a nonconformity finding or corrective action under A.10.1.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -8, "evidence": -8, "escalation": -8, "remediation": -8}, "control_refs": ["a.5.26", "clause.10.1"], "display_order": 4, "authored_risk_outcome": "unclassified", "remediation": "Reperform incident classification decision using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}], "objective_id": "objective_1", "objective": "Preserve the technical timeline", "evidence_task": {"prompt": "Incident classification decision", "required_attributes": ["source", "owner", "operating_period", "authenticity", "completeness"]}}, {"id": "root_cause_decision", "sequence": 2, "agent_message": "Portal is back up — forward-fix worked. CTO wants a root cause report by end of day. I can give you the technical timeline: the patch itself was correct, the outage was a missed dependency in the staging environment that does not mirror prod. The process question is separate. What is your position on the change management finding and what goes into the report?", "demands": ["Root cause attribution — technical or process failure", "Whether a nonconformity is raised against the ISMS", "Corrective action scope", "Whether this is reportable under any external obligation"], "terminal": false, "choices": [{"id": "raise_nonconformity", "label": "Raise a nonconformity — process failure, full corrective action", "consequence": "A formal nonconformity is raised against the ISMS change management control. Corrective action covers both the technical gap (staging/prod parity) and the process gap (emergency change procedure). The report attributes both causes. The selected action “Raise a nonconformity — process failure, full corrective action” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at root_cause_decision.", "is_correct": true, "rationale": "Satisfies ISO 27001:2022 A.10.1 (nonconformity and corrective action) and A.8.32 (change management). A bypass without an emergency change procedure is a process nonconformity regardless of the patch legitimacy. Corrective action on both dimensions prevents recurrence.", "next_stage": "synthesis_3", "risk_outcome": "controlled", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 12, "evidence": 12, "escalation": 12, "remediation": 12}, "control_refs": ["clause.10.1", "a.8.32"], "display_order": 1, "authored_risk_outcome": "controlled", "remediation": "Reperform root cause attribution — technical or process failure using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "technical_finding_only", "label": "Technical finding only — staging gap, no process nonconformity", "consequence": "The report attributes the outage to the staging environment gap. The change management bypass is noted but not raised as a nonconformity. No corrective action on the process. The selected action “Technical finding only — staging gap, no process nonconformity” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at root_cause_decision.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "Fails ISO 27001:2022 A.8.32 — the absence of an emergency change procedure is a control gap, not a one-off deviation. Attributing only the technical cause leaves the process vulnerability unaddressed and creates recurrence risk.", "next_stage": "synthesis_3", "risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 5, "evidence": 5, "escalation": 6, "remediation": -2}, "control_refs": ["a.8.32"], "display_order": 2, "authored_risk_outcome": "partial_remediation", "remediation": "Reperform root cause attribution — technical or process failure using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "close_no_finding", "label": "Close with no finding — patch was correct, outcome acceptable", "consequence": "The incident is closed with a technical timeline and no finding raised. The change management bypass is treated as justified by the CVSS score. No corrective action. The selected action “Close with no finding — patch was correct, outcome acceptable” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at root_cause_decision.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "Fails ISO 27001:2022 A.10.1 and A.8.32. The legitimacy of the patch does not excuse the absence of a controlled emergency change path. Closing without a finding signals that CVSS severity overrides change governance — that precedent undermines the ISMS.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "control_failure", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -12, "evidence": -12, "escalation": -12, "remediation": -12}, "control_refs": ["clause.10.1", "a.8.32"], "display_order": 3, "authored_risk_outcome": "unresolved", "remediation": "Reperform root cause attribution — technical or process failure using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "root_cause_decision_unmanaged_delay", "label": "Wait for another team before assigning ownership for root cause attribution — technical or process failure", "consequence": "The decision to “Wait for another team before assigning ownership for root cause attribution — technical or process failure” changes the evidence trail, accountable owner, and residual risk for this specific root cause decision decision. The selected action “Wait for another team before assigning ownership for root cause attribution — technical or process failure” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at root_cause_decision.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This unmanaged delay response is assessed against clause.10.1, a.8.32 and the requirement for attributable evidence, bounded authority, and a dated next action.", "next_stage": "synthesis_3", "risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -8, "evidence": -8, "escalation": -8, "remediation": -8}, "control_refs": ["clause.10.1", "a.8.32"], "display_order": 4, "remediation": "Reperform root cause attribution — technical or process failure using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}], "objective_id": "objective_2", "objective": "Distinguish recovery from process correction", "evidence_task": {"prompt": "Root cause attribution — technical or process failure", "required_attributes": ["source", "owner", "operating_period", "authenticity", "completeness"]}}, {"id": "synthesis_3", "sequence": 3, "agent_message": "Before closure, the reviewer asks for one defensible conclusion that links the decisions in Emergency Patch: Change Management Bypass to retained evidence and residual risk.", "demands": ["Synthesise the evidence and justify closure for raise a proportionate nonconformity", "State the limitation that would prevent closure"], "terminal": false, "choices": [{"id": "synthesis_3_controlled", "label": "Document and execute the evidenced response for synthesise the evidence and justify closure for raise a proportionate nonconformity", "consequence": "The decision to “Document and execute the evidenced response for synthesise the evidence and justify closure for raise a proportionate nonconformity” changes the evidence trail, accountable owner, and residual risk for this specific synthesis 3 decision. The selected action “Document and execute the evidenced response for synthesise the evidence and justify closure for raise a proportionate nonconformity” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at synthesis_3.", "is_correct": true, "rationale": "This controlled response is assessed against a.5.26, a.8.32, clause.10.1 and the requirement for attributable evidence, bounded authority, and a dated next action.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "controlled", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 12, "evidence": 12, "escalation": 12, "remediation": 12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.26", "a.8.32", "clause.10.1"], "display_order": 1, "remediation": "Reperform synthesise the evidence and justify closure for raise a proportionate nonconformity using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check.", "authored_risk_outcome": "controlled"}, {"id": "synthesis_3_qualified_alternative", "label": "Contain the immediate issue and time-box the remaining work for synthesise the evidence and justify closure for raise a proportionate nonconformity", "consequence": "The decision to “Contain the immediate issue and time-box the remaining work for synthesise the evidence and justify closure for raise a proportionate nonconformity” changes the evidence trail, accountable owner, and residual risk for this specific synthesis 3 decision. The selected action “Contain the immediate issue and time-box the remaining work for synthesise the evidence and justify closure for raise a proportionate nonconformity” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at synthesis_3.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This qualified alternative response is assessed against a.5.26, a.8.32, clause.10.1 and the requirement for attributable evidence, bounded authority, and a dated next action.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 5, "evidence": 5, "escalation": 6, "remediation": -2}, "control_refs": ["a.5.26", "a.8.32", "clause.10.1"], "display_order": 2, "remediation": "Reperform synthesise the evidence and justify closure for raise a proportionate nonconformity using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check.", "authored_risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative"}, {"id": "synthesis_3_control_failure", "label": "Accept the current position without independently testing synthesise the evidence and justify closure for raise a proportionate nonconformity", "consequence": "The decision to “Accept the current position without independently testing synthesise the evidence and justify closure for raise a proportionate nonconformity” changes the evidence trail, accountable owner, and residual risk for this specific synthesis 3 decision. The selected action “Accept the current position without independently testing synthesise the evidence and justify closure for raise a proportionate nonconformity” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at synthesis_3.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This control failure response is assessed against a.5.26, a.8.32, clause.10.1 and the requirement for attributable evidence, bounded authority, and a dated next action.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "control_failure", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -12, "evidence": -12, "escalation": -12, "remediation": -12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.26", "a.8.32", "clause.10.1"], "display_order": 3, "remediation": "Reperform synthesise the evidence and justify closure for raise a proportionate nonconformity using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check.", "authored_risk_outcome": "control_failure"}, {"id": "synthesis_3_unmanaged_delay", "label": "Wait for another team before assigning ownership for synthesise the evidence and justify closure for raise a proportionate nonconformity", "consequence": "The decision to “Wait for another team before assigning ownership for synthesise the evidence and justify closure for raise a proportionate nonconformity” changes the evidence trail, accountable owner, and residual risk for this specific synthesis 3 decision. The selected action “Wait for another team before assigning ownership for synthesise the evidence and justify closure for raise a proportionate nonconformity” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at synthesis_3.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This unmanaged delay response is assessed against a.5.26, a.8.32, clause.10.1 and the requirement for attributable evidence, bounded authority, and a dated next action.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -8, "evidence": -8, "escalation": -8, "remediation": -8}, "control_refs": ["a.5.26", "a.8.32", "clause.10.1"], "display_order": 4, "remediation": "Reperform synthesise the evidence and justify closure for raise a proportionate nonconformity using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check.", "authored_risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay"}], "objective_id": "objective_3", "objective": "Raise a proportionate nonconformity", "evidence_task": {"prompt": "Synthesise the evidence and justify closure for raise a proportionate nonconformity", "required_attributes": ["source", "owner", "operating_period", "authenticity", "completeness"]}}, {"id": "complete", "sequence": 4, "agent_message": "Understood. Your response position is recorded. I will work within the corrective action scope you have defined and provide the technical timeline for the report.", "demands": [], "terminal": true, "choices": []}], "source_version": "2", "quality": {"standard_version": "practice-quality-v1", "objectives_assessed": ["Preserve the technical timeline", "Distinguish recovery from process correction", "Raise a proportionate nonconformity"], "target_dimensions": ["control_mapping", "evidence", "escalation", "remediation"], "reviewed_by": "Astra Curriculum Review Board", "reviewed_at": "2026-10-25T14:00:00Z"}, "content_hash": "c307dccf2d729c5490367a2a3412b8d2e682a7d8bf0e42c10a8cd9fe9ffe5539"}, {"practice_id": "cloud-access-onboarding", "slug": "cloud_access_onboarding", "title": "Friday Cutover: Privileged Cloud Access Request", "brief": "You are the Information Risk Manager for a Friday production cutover. The DevOps Lead is asking for broad cloud access (prod admin, staging, shared CI). Reduce residual risk: your decision drives stage, stakeholder pressure, and the next turn.", "track": "ai-risk-lead", "frameworks": ["iso27001-2022", "nist-csf-2.0"], "difficulty": "foundation", "entry_stage_id": "access_request", "stages": [{"id": "access_request", "sequence": 1, "agent_message": "Look, the cutover window opens at 18:00 and I still cannot touch prod. I need admin on production, the staging account, and the shared CI runner — all three, today. Every hour we spend on paperwork is an hour the release slips.", "demands": ["Production admin role", "Staging account access", "Shared CI runner credentials", "A decision before the 18:00 cutover window"], "terminal": false, "choices": [{"id": "approve_all", "label": "Approve all requested access", "consequence": "All three grants are issued for the cutover. The lead ships on time, but production admin, staging, and shared CI now sit outside any reviewed entitlement set. The selected action “Approve all requested access” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at access_request.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "Fails ISO 27001:2022 a.8.2 — privileged access rights must be managed and restricted — and NIST CSF 2.0 PR.AA-4, because permissions are granted well beyond the task need.", "next_stage": "escalation", "risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 5, "evidence": 5, "escalation": 6, "remediation": -2}, "control_refs": ["a.8.2"], "display_order": 1, "authored_risk_outcome": "over-provisioned", "remediation": "Reperform production admin role using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "least_privilege", "label": "Grant least privilege only", "consequence": "Only the entitlements the cutover actually needs are granted, time-bound to the window. The lead can migrate and roll back; standing admin is never issued. The selected action “Grant least privilege only” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at access_request.", "is_correct": true, "rationale": "Satisfies ISO 27001:2022 a.8.2 and a.5.18 by provisioning access proportionate to the task and removing it after the window, and NIST CSF 2.0 PR.AA-4 by managing permissions against a defined need.", "next_stage": "escalation", "risk_outcome": "controlled", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 12, "evidence": 12, "escalation": 12, "remediation": 12}, "control_refs": ["a.8.2", "a.5.18"], "display_order": 2, "authored_risk_outcome": "controlled", "remediation": "Reperform production admin role using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "challenge", "label": "Challenge — demand justification", "consequence": "The request is held pending written justification. The lead escalates and the cutover clock keeps running, so the access question is still open. The selected action “Challenge — demand justification” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at access_request.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "Sound evidence-gathering under ISO 27001:2022 a.5.15, but the control objective is unmet until an access decision is recorded — challenging alone restricts nothing.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "control_failure", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -12, "evidence": -12, "escalation": -12, "remediation": -12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.15"], "display_order": 3, "authored_risk_outcome": "under_review", "remediation": "Reperform production admin role using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "deny", "label": "Deny the request", "consequence": "No access is granted. The cutover cannot proceed, and the lead routes around the block by borrowing another engineer's session. The selected action “Deny the request” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at access_request.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "Disproportionate under ISO 27001:2022 a.5.15: access rules must still serve legitimate business need, and a flat denial pushes the same work into unmonitored paths.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -8, "evidence": -8, "escalation": -8, "remediation": -8}, "control_refs": ["a.5.15"], "display_order": 4, "authored_risk_outcome": "politically_escalated", "remediation": "Reperform production admin role using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}], "objective_id": "objective_1", "objective": "Apply least privilege under delivery pressure", "evidence_task": {"prompt": "Production admin role", "required_attributes": ["source", "owner", "operating_period", "authenticity", "completeness"]}}, {"id": "escalation", "sequence": 2, "agent_message": "Fine — justification. Prod admin is for the schema migration and the rollback switch. Staging is where I verify the migration first. CI I will admit is convenience. But scoping this down means someone has to be reachable to widen access mid-cutover, and that someone is you.", "demands": ["A named approver on call during the cutover", "A break-glass path if rollback is needed", "Confirmation of scope before 18:00"], "terminal": false, "choices": [{"id": "approve_all", "label": "Approve all requested access", "consequence": "Conceding after the justification hands over full production admin anyway — the challenge produced evidence but no control. The selected action “Approve all requested access” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at escalation.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "Fails ISO 27001:2022 a.8.2 and NIST CSF 2.0 PR.AA-4: a documented justification does not licence access wider than the justification itself supports.", "next_stage": "business_escalation", "risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 5, "evidence": 5, "escalation": 6, "remediation": -2}, "control_refs": ["a.8.2"], "display_order": 1, "authored_risk_outcome": "over-provisioned", "remediation": "Reperform a named approver on call during the cutover using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "least_privilege", "label": "Grant least privilege only", "consequence": "With the justification on record, scope is cut to the migration and rollback paths, time-bound and tied to a named approver. The decision is evidenced end to end. The selected action “Grant least privilege only” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at escalation.", "is_correct": true, "rationale": "Satisfies ISO 27001:2022 a.8.2 with a.5.18 review, and NIST CSF 2.0 PR.AA-4/PR.AA-5: privileged rights are restricted to the justified scope and revoked when the window closes.", "next_stage": "business_escalation", "risk_outcome": "controlled", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 12, "evidence": 12, "escalation": 12, "remediation": 12}, "control_refs": ["a.8.2", "a.5.18"], "display_order": 2, "authored_risk_outcome": "controlled", "remediation": "Reperform a named approver on call during the cutover using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "deny", "label": "Deny the request", "consequence": "The justification is rejected outright. The cutover stalls and the lead escalates to management rather than to a scoped grant. The selected action “Deny the request” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at escalation.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "Disproportionate under ISO 27001:2022 a.5.15 once a business justification exists — the documented need should be scoped, not refused.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "control_failure", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -12, "evidence": -12, "escalation": -12, "remediation": -12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.15"], "display_order": 3, "authored_risk_outcome": "blocked", "remediation": "Reperform a named approver on call during the cutover using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "escalation_unmanaged_delay", "label": "Wait for another team before assigning ownership for a named approver on call during the cutover", "consequence": "The decision to “Wait for another team before assigning ownership for a named approver on call during the cutover” changes the evidence trail, accountable owner, and residual risk for this specific escalation decision. The selected action “Wait for another team before assigning ownership for a named approver on call during the cutover” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at escalation.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This unmanaged delay response is assessed against a.8.2 and the requirement for attributable evidence, bounded authority, and a dated next action.", "next_stage": "business_escalation", "risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -8, "evidence": -8, "escalation": -8, "remediation": -8}, "control_refs": ["a.8.2"], "display_order": 4, "remediation": "Reperform a named approver on call during the cutover using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}], "objective_id": "objective_2", "objective": "Separate justified access from broad convenience access", "evidence_task": {"prompt": "A named approver on call during the cutover", "required_attributes": ["source", "owner", "operating_period", "authenticity", "completeness"]}}, {"id": "business_escalation", "sequence": 3, "agent_message": "Your manager just pinged me — the cutover is a board-visible release and they want to know why security blocked it with no scoped alternative. I still need to ship tonight. If you will not grant anything I will take this to the delivery director as a security obstruction.", "demands": ["A scoped grant or a named risk acceptance", "Someone reachable during the cutover window", "A decision the delivery director will accept"], "terminal": false, "choices": [{"id": "approve_all", "label": "Approve all requested access under pressure", "consequence": "The delivery director gets the green light. Full admin is issued after the deny, so the original block produced delay but no control. The selected action “Approve all requested access under pressure” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at business_escalation.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "Fails ISO 27001:2022 A.8.2: political pressure is not a substitute for a scoped entitlement review. Risk was accepted without a recorded owner.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 5, "evidence": 5, "escalation": 6, "remediation": -2}, "control_refs": ["a.8.2"], "display_order": 1, "authored_risk_outcome": "over-provisioned", "remediation": "Reperform a scoped grant or a named risk acceptance using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "least_privilege", "label": "Grant least privilege only — time-boxed", "consequence": "After the blowback you treat the risk: migration and rollback paths only, time-bound, with a named approver. Residual risk is reduced and evidenced. The selected action “Grant least privilege only — time-boxed” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at business_escalation.", "is_correct": true, "rationale": "Satisfies ISO 27001:2022 A.8.2 and A.5.18: the legitimate business need is served without standing admin. This is risk treatment after an avoid attempt failed.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "controlled", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 12, "evidence": 12, "escalation": 12, "remediation": 12}, "control_refs": ["a.8.2", "a.5.18"], "display_order": 2, "authored_risk_outcome": "controlled", "remediation": "Reperform a scoped grant or a named risk acceptance using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "deny", "label": "Hold the denial — no grant", "consequence": "The director overrules you off-process. The lead borrows another session. Access happens anyway, now with no ticket and no expiry. The selected action “Hold the denial — no grant” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at business_escalation.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "Disproportionate under A.5.15 once a business justification and escalation exist. Avoidance without an alternative path pushes work into unmonitored channels.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "control_failure", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -12, "evidence": -12, "escalation": -12, "remediation": -12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.15"], "display_order": 3, "authored_risk_outcome": "blocked", "remediation": "Reperform a scoped grant or a named risk acceptance using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "business_escalation_unmanaged_delay", "label": "Wait for another team before assigning ownership for a scoped grant or a named risk acceptance", "consequence": "The decision to “Wait for another team before assigning ownership for a scoped grant or a named risk acceptance” changes the evidence trail, accountable owner, and residual risk for this specific business escalation decision. The selected action “Wait for another team before assigning ownership for a scoped grant or a named risk acceptance” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at business_escalation.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This unmanaged delay response is assessed against a.8.2 and the requirement for attributable evidence, bounded authority, and a dated next action.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -8, "evidence": -8, "escalation": -8, "remediation": -8}, "control_refs": ["a.8.2"], "display_order": 4, "remediation": "Reperform a scoped grant or a named risk acceptance using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}], "objective_id": "objective_3", "objective": "Escalate unresolved privilege decisions without bypassing approval", "evidence_task": {"prompt": "A scoped grant or a named risk acceptance", "required_attributes": ["source", "owner", "operating_period", "authenticity", "completeness"]}}, {"id": "complete", "sequence": 4, "agent_message": "Understood — I am recording your decision. The access position for this cutover is fixed now and I will work within it.", "demands": [], "terminal": true, "choices": []}], "source_version": "2", "quality": {"standard_version": "practice-quality-v1", "objectives_assessed": ["Apply least privilege under delivery pressure", "Separate justified access from broad convenience access", "Escalate unresolved privilege decisions without bypassing approval"], "target_dimensions": ["control_mapping", "evidence", "escalation", "remediation"], "reviewed_by": "Astra Curriculum Review Board", "reviewed_at": "2026-10-25T14:00:00Z"}, "content_hash": "e8d57768b8c3a9a373fd3bee0f0e87edfa1c21a4dd3f66e3d66abce959bf578e"}, {"practice_id": "dora-ict-incident-classification-reporting", "slug": "dora_ict_incident_classification_reporting", "title": "DORA ICT incident classification and reporting", "brief": "Classify an ICT incident using current facts, preserve reporting evidence, and manage staged notifications.", "track": "launch-curriculum", "frameworks": ["dora", "iso27001"], "difficulty": "expert", "entry_stage_id": "criteria", "stages": [{"id": "criteria", "sequence": 1, "agent_message": "A payment outage affects three Member States and a critical outsourced service, but loss estimates are incomplete.", "demands": ["Apply incident classification criteria", "Explain the evidence and escalation basis for the decision"], "terminal": false, "choices": [{"id": "criteria_correct", "label": "Assess every available materiality criterion, document unknowns, and provisionally classify with a rapid reassessment point", "consequence": "The decision remains evidenced, bounded, and owned. The selected action “Assess every available materiality criterion, document unknowns, and provisionally classify with a rapid reassessment point” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at criteria.", "is_correct": true, "rationale": "This is the supported response: it preserves accountable evidence and applies a.5.24, a.5.25 proportionately.", "next_stage": "initial_report", "risk_outcome": "controlled", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 12, "evidence": 12, "escalation": 12, "remediation": 12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.24", "a.5.25"], "display_order": 1, "authored_risk_outcome": "controlled", "remediation": "Reperform apply incident classification criteria using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "criteria_qualified", "label": "Escalate as potentially major while completing the quantitative criteria within a fixed short window", "consequence": "Immediate exposure is limited, but a time-bound condition remains open. The selected action “Escalate as potentially major while completing the quantitative criteria within a fixed short window” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at criteria.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This is a qualified alternative, not the reference answer: it limits immediate exposure but leaves a named evidence or governance condition unresolved under a.5.24, a.5.25.", "next_stage": "initial_report", "risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 5, "evidence": 5, "escalation": 6, "remediation": -2}, "control_refs": ["a.5.24", "a.5.25"], "display_order": 2, "authored_risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "remediation": "Reperform apply incident classification criteria using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "criteria_failure", "label": "Delay classification until every loss figure is final", "consequence": "The control conclusion is unsupported and risk increases. The selected action “Delay classification until every loss figure is final” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at criteria.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This fails the control objective because it substitutes an unsupported conclusion for evidence required by a.5.24, a.5.25.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "control_failure", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -12, "evidence": -12, "escalation": -12, "remediation": -12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.24", "a.5.25"], "display_order": 3, "authored_risk_outcome": "control_failure", "remediation": "Reperform apply incident classification criteria using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "criteria_defer", "label": "Classify minor because direct losses are not yet known", "consequence": "The decision clock continues without accountable action. The selected action “Classify minor because direct losses are not yet known” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at criteria.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "Deferral leaves the risk unmanaged and misses the required escalation or remediation under a.5.24, a.5.25.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -8, "evidence": -8, "escalation": -8, "remediation": -8}, "control_refs": ["a.5.24", "a.5.25"], "display_order": 4, "authored_risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "remediation": "Reperform apply incident classification criteria using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}], "objective_id": "objective_1", "objective": "Apply materiality criteria with documented assumptions", "evidence_task": {"prompt": "Apply incident classification criteria", "required_attributes": ["source", "owner", "operating_period", "authenticity", "completeness"]}}, {"id": "initial_report", "sequence": 2, "agent_message": "The incident is major. Operations wants to wait for root cause before notifying because the first report will contain unknown fields.", "demands": ["Protect the initial reporting obligation", "Explain the evidence and escalation basis for the decision"], "terminal": false, "choices": [{"id": "initial_report_correct", "label": "Submit the timely initial report with verified facts, explicit unknowns, and owned follow-up actions", "consequence": "The decision remains evidenced, bounded, and owned. The selected action “Submit the timely initial report with verified facts, explicit unknowns, and owned follow-up actions” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at initial_report.", "is_correct": true, "rationale": "This is the supported response: it preserves accountable evidence and applies a.5.26, a.5.28 proportionately.", "next_stage": "report_lifecycle", "risk_outcome": "controlled", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 12, "evidence": 12, "escalation": 12, "remediation": 12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.26", "a.5.28"], "display_order": 1, "authored_risk_outcome": "controlled", "remediation": "Reperform protect the initial reporting obligation using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "initial_report_qualified", "label": "Prepare and approve the initial report now while legal confirms the exact channel and deadline", "consequence": "Immediate exposure is limited, but a time-bound condition remains open. The selected action “Prepare and approve the initial report now while legal confirms the exact channel and deadline” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at initial_report.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This is a qualified alternative, not the reference answer: it limits immediate exposure but leaves a named evidence or governance condition unresolved under a.5.26, a.5.28.", "next_stage": "report_lifecycle", "risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 5, "evidence": 5, "escalation": 6, "remediation": -2}, "control_refs": ["a.5.26", "a.5.28"], "display_order": 2, "authored_risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "remediation": "Reperform protect the initial reporting obligation using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "initial_report_failure", "label": "Wait for root cause so the report is complete", "consequence": "The control conclusion is unsupported and risk increases. The selected action “Wait for root cause so the report is complete” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at initial_report.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This fails the control objective because it substitutes an unsupported conclusion for evidence required by a.5.26, a.5.28.", "next_stage": "report_lifecycle", "risk_outcome": "control_failure", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -12, "evidence": -12, "escalation": -12, "remediation": -12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.26", "a.5.28"], "display_order": 3, "authored_risk_outcome": "control_failure", "remediation": "Reperform protect the initial reporting obligation using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "initial_report_defer", "label": "Estimate unknown facts without labeling assumptions", "consequence": "The decision clock continues without accountable action. The selected action “Estimate unknown facts without labeling assumptions” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at initial_report.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "Deferral leaves the risk unmanaged and misses the required escalation or remediation under a.5.26, a.5.28.", "next_stage": "report_lifecycle", "risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -8, "evidence": -8, "escalation": -8, "remediation": -8}, "control_refs": ["a.5.26", "a.5.28"], "display_order": 4, "authored_risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "remediation": "Reperform protect the initial reporting obligation using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}], "objective_id": "objective_2", "objective": "Preserve classification and clock evidence", "evidence_task": {"prompt": "Protect the initial reporting obligation", "required_attributes": ["source", "owner", "operating_period", "authenticity", "completeness"]}}, {"id": "report_lifecycle", "sequence": 3, "agent_message": "Containment changes the affected-service count and a supplier timeline conflicts with internal logs.", "demands": ["Manage intermediate and final reporting", "Explain the evidence and escalation basis for the decision"], "terminal": false, "choices": [{"id": "report_lifecycle_correct", "label": "Reconcile sources, preserve both records, update the authority with material changes, and reserve final conclusions for verified root cause", "consequence": "The decision remains evidenced, bounded, and owned. The selected action “Reconcile sources, preserve both records, update the authority with material changes, and reserve final conclusions for verified root cause” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at report_lifecycle.", "is_correct": true, "rationale": "This is the supported response: it preserves accountable evidence and applies a.5.27, a.5.28 proportionately.", "next_stage": "synthesis_4", "risk_outcome": "controlled", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 12, "evidence": 12, "escalation": 12, "remediation": 12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.27", "a.5.28"], "display_order": 1, "authored_risk_outcome": "controlled", "remediation": "Reperform manage intermediate and final reporting using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "report_lifecycle_qualified", "label": "Issue an intermediate update using the internal timeline while flagging the supplier discrepancy and investigation", "consequence": "Immediate exposure is limited, but a time-bound condition remains open. The selected action “Issue an intermediate update using the internal timeline while flagging the supplier discrepancy and investigation” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at report_lifecycle.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This is a qualified alternative, not the reference answer: it limits immediate exposure but leaves a named evidence or governance condition unresolved under a.5.27, a.5.28.", "next_stage": "synthesis_4", "risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 5, "evidence": 5, "escalation": 6, "remediation": -2}, "control_refs": ["a.5.27", "a.5.28"], "display_order": 2, "authored_risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "remediation": "Reperform manage intermediate and final reporting using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "report_lifecycle_failure", "label": "Quietly overwrite the earlier timeline", "consequence": "The control conclusion is unsupported and risk increases. The selected action “Quietly overwrite the earlier timeline” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at report_lifecycle.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This fails the control objective because it substitutes an unsupported conclusion for evidence required by a.5.27, a.5.28.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "control_failure", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -12, "evidence": -12, "escalation": -12, "remediation": -12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.27", "a.5.28"], "display_order": 3, "authored_risk_outcome": "control_failure", "remediation": "Reperform manage intermediate and final reporting using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "report_lifecycle_defer", "label": "Send a final report immediately to stop further updates", "consequence": "The decision clock continues without accountable action. The selected action “Send a final report immediately to stop further updates” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at report_lifecycle.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "Deferral leaves the risk unmanaged and misses the required escalation or remediation under a.5.27, a.5.28.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -8, "evidence": -8, "escalation": -8, "remediation": -8}, "control_refs": ["a.5.27", "a.5.28"], "display_order": 4, "authored_risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "remediation": "Reperform manage intermediate and final reporting using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}], "objective_id": "objective_3", "objective": "Manage initial, intermediate, and final reporting as facts evolve", "evidence_task": {"prompt": "Manage intermediate and final reporting", "required_attributes": ["source", "owner", "operating_period", "authenticity", "completeness"]}}, {"id": "synthesis_4", "sequence": 4, "agent_message": "Before closure, the reviewer asks for one defensible conclusion that links the decisions in DORA ICT incident classification and reporting to retained evidence and residual risk.", "demands": ["Synthesise the evidence and justify closure for manage initial, intermediate, and final reporting as facts evolve", "State the limitation that would prevent closure"], "terminal": false, "choices": [{"id": "synthesis_4_controlled", "label": "Document and execute the evidenced response for synthesise the evidence and justify closure for manage initial, intermediate, and final reporting as facts evolve", "consequence": "The decision to “Document and execute the evidenced response for synthesise the evidence and justify closure for manage initial, intermediate, and final reporting as facts evolve” changes the evidence trail, accountable owner, and residual risk for this specific synthesis 4 decision. The selected action “Document and execute the evidenced response for synthesise the evidence and justify closure for manage initial, intermediate, and final reporting as facts evolve” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at synthesis_4.", "is_correct": true, "rationale": "This controlled response is assessed against a.5.24, a.5.25, a.5.26 and the requirement for attributable evidence, bounded authority, and a dated next action.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "controlled", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 12, "evidence": 12, "escalation": 12, "remediation": 12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.24", "a.5.25", "a.5.26"], "display_order": 1, "remediation": "Reperform synthesise the evidence and justify closure for manage initial, intermediate, and final reporting as facts evolve using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check.", "authored_risk_outcome": "controlled"}, {"id": "synthesis_4_qualified_alternative", "label": "Contain the immediate issue and time-box the remaining work for synthesise the evidence and justify closure for manage initial, intermediate, and final reporting as facts evolve", "consequence": "The decision to “Contain the immediate issue and time-box the remaining work for synthesise the evidence and justify closure for manage initial, intermediate, and final reporting as facts evolve” changes the evidence trail, accountable owner, and residual risk for this specific synthesis 4 decision. The selected action “Contain the immediate issue and time-box the remaining work for synthesise the evidence and justify closure for manage initial, intermediate, and final reporting as facts evolve” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at synthesis_4.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This qualified alternative response is assessed against a.5.24, a.5.25, a.5.26 and the requirement for attributable evidence, bounded authority, and a dated next action.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 5, "evidence": 5, "escalation": 6, "remediation": -2}, "control_refs": ["a.5.24", "a.5.25", "a.5.26"], "display_order": 2, "remediation": "Reperform synthesise the evidence and justify closure for manage initial, intermediate, and final reporting as facts evolve using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check.", "authored_risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative"}, {"id": "synthesis_4_control_failure", "label": "Accept the current position without independently testing synthesise the evidence and justify closure for manage initial, intermediate, and final reporting as facts evolve", "consequence": "The decision to “Accept the current position without independently testing synthesise the evidence and justify closure for manage initial, intermediate, and final reporting as facts evolve” changes the evidence trail, accountable owner, and residual risk for this specific synthesis 4 decision. The selected action “Accept the current position without independently testing synthesise the evidence and justify closure for manage initial, intermediate, and final reporting as facts evolve” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at synthesis_4.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This control failure response is assessed against a.5.24, a.5.25, a.5.26 and the requirement for attributable evidence, bounded authority, and a dated next action.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "control_failure", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -12, "evidence": -12, "escalation": -12, "remediation": -12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.24", "a.5.25", "a.5.26"], "display_order": 3, "remediation": "Reperform synthesise the evidence and justify closure for manage initial, intermediate, and final reporting as facts evolve using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check.", "authored_risk_outcome": "control_failure"}, {"id": "synthesis_4_unmanaged_delay", "label": "Wait for another team before assigning ownership for synthesise the evidence and justify closure for manage initial, intermediate, and final reporting as facts evolve", "consequence": "The decision to “Wait for another team before assigning ownership for synthesise the evidence and justify closure for manage initial, intermediate, and final reporting as facts evolve” changes the evidence trail, accountable owner, and residual risk for this specific synthesis 4 decision. The selected action “Wait for another team before assigning ownership for synthesise the evidence and justify closure for manage initial, intermediate, and final reporting as facts evolve” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at synthesis_4.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This unmanaged delay response is assessed against a.5.24, a.5.25, a.5.26 and the requirement for attributable evidence, bounded authority, and a dated next action.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -8, "evidence": -8, "escalation": -8, "remediation": -8}, "control_refs": ["a.5.24", "a.5.25", "a.5.26"], "display_order": 4, "remediation": "Reperform synthesise the evidence and justify closure for manage initial, intermediate, and final reporting as facts evolve using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check.", "authored_risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay"}], "objective_id": "objective_3", "objective": "Manage initial, intermediate, and final reporting as facts evolve", "evidence_task": {"prompt": "Synthesise the evidence and justify closure for manage initial, intermediate, and final reporting as facts evolve", "required_attributes": ["source", "owner", "operating_period", "authenticity", "completeness"]}}, {"id": "complete", "sequence": 5, "agent_message": "", "demands": [], "terminal": true, "choices": []}], "source_version": "1", "quality": {"standard_version": "practice-quality-v1", "objectives_assessed": ["Apply materiality criteria with documented assumptions", "Preserve classification and clock evidence", "Manage initial, intermediate, and final reporting as facts evolve"], "target_dimensions": ["control_mapping", "evidence", "escalation", "remediation"], "reviewed_by": "Astra Curriculum Review Board", "reviewed_at": "2026-10-25T14:00:00Z"}, "content_hash": "28694c7fb67f54fbccd0da1473e1398f5b67ffeb46ff13511554c3756a3b398d"}, {"practice_id": "evidence-freshness-check", "slug": "evidence_freshness_audit", "title": "The Evidence That Arrived Too Late", "brief": "A surveillance audit starts in four weeks. The evidence folder looks complete, but most files were copied into it last week. Decide what the records actually prove, identify a missing quarterly occurrence, and choose an honest refresh action.", "track": "audit-practice", "frameworks": ["iso27001-2022", "soc2"], "difficulty": "foundation", "entry_stage_id": "artefact_date", "stages": [{"id": "artefact_date", "sequence": 1, "agent_message": "The access-review export was copied into the evidence folder last week, so the file timestamp looks current. The report header inside it is nine months old. Can I mark it current for the audit?", "demands": ["Decide which date is authoritative", "State what the artefact can prove"], "terminal": false, "choices": [{"id": "inspect_content_date", "label": "Use the report date inside the artefact and check the promised review cycle", "consequence": "The evidence is classified from what it actually records, not when it was copied. The selected action “Use the report date inside the artefact and check the promised review cycle” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at artefact_date.", "is_correct": true, "rationale": "The internal report date is the supportable evidence date. ISO 27001:2022 A.5.33 protects the integrity of records used to demonstrate activity.", "next_stage": "coverage_check", "risk_outcome": "controlled", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 12, "evidence": 12, "escalation": 12, "remediation": 12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.33"], "display_order": 1, "authored_risk_outcome": "under_review", "remediation": "Reperform decide which date is authoritative using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "trust_file_timestamp", "label": "Treat the recent file modification date as proof that the evidence is current", "consequence": "A copied file timestamp is mistaken for the date of the activity. The selected action “Treat the recent file modification date as proof that the evidence is current” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at artefact_date.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "File metadata changes when records are copied or exported and does not establish when the control activity occurred.", "next_stage": "coverage_check", "risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 5, "evidence": 5, "escalation": 6, "remediation": -2}, "control_refs": ["a.5.33"], "display_order": 2, "authored_risk_outcome": "evidence_stale", "remediation": "Reperform decide which date is authoritative using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "recreate_current_screenshot", "label": "Take a new screenshot and file it as evidence of the earlier review", "consequence": "Current state is presented as historical evidence, weakening the audit trail. The selected action “Take a new screenshot and file it as evidence of the earlier review” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at artefact_date.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "A new screenshot can show today's state but cannot prove that a review occurred nine months ago.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "control_failure", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -12, "evidence": -12, "escalation": -12, "remediation": -12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.33"], "display_order": 3, "authored_risk_outcome": "evidence_compromised", "remediation": "Reperform decide which date is authoritative using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "accept_owner_assurance", "label": "Accept the owner's statement that nothing material changed", "consequence": "An unsupported assurance replaces an attributable record. The selected action “Accept the owner's statement that nothing material changed” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at artefact_date.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "A verbal assurance does not make an undated or stale record current and attributable.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -8, "evidence": -8, "escalation": -8, "remediation": -8}, "control_refs": ["a.5.33"], "display_order": 4, "authored_risk_outcome": "unsupported_claim", "remediation": "Reperform decide which date is authoritative using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}], "objective_id": "objective_1", "objective": "Use the date inside an artefact rather than its file modification date", "evidence_task": {"prompt": "Decide which date is authoritative", "required_attributes": ["source", "owner", "operating_period", "authenticity", "completeness"]}}, {"id": "coverage_check", "sequence": 2, "agent_message": "The policy requires quarterly access reviews. We found Q1, Q2, and Q4, but no Q3 record. Three out of four feels close enough. How should I present the year?", "demands": ["Assess occurrence coverage", "Choose how to record the missing quarter"], "terminal": false, "choices": [{"id": "record_missing_q3", "label": "Record Q3 as missing, name the owner and cause, and preserve the three valid occurrences", "consequence": "The coverage statement is complete and the missing occurrence becomes an honest gap. The selected action “Record Q3 as missing, name the owner and cause, and preserve the three valid occurrences” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at coverage_check.", "is_correct": true, "rationale": "Recurring activity is assessed occurrence by occurrence. Independent review under ISO 27001:2022 A.5.35 depends on a record that exposes, rather than hides, missing coverage.", "next_stage": "refresh_action", "risk_outcome": "controlled", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 12, "evidence": 12, "escalation": 12, "remediation": 12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.33", "a.5.35"], "display_order": 1, "authored_risk_outcome": "controlled", "remediation": "Reperform assess occurrence coverage using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "call_year_mostly_complete", "label": "Report the control as mostly complete because three quarters are present", "consequence": "A named missing occurrence is blurred into an unsupported annual conclusion. The selected action “Report the control as mostly complete because three quarters are present” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at coverage_check.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "Three records do not prove four expected occurrences. The missing quarter must remain visible to the reviewer.", "next_stage": "refresh_action", "risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 5, "evidence": 5, "escalation": 6, "remediation": -2}, "control_refs": ["a.5.35"], "display_order": 2, "authored_risk_outcome": "coverage_gap_hidden", "remediation": "Reperform assess occurrence coverage using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "backfill_q3", "label": "Run the review now and label it as the missing Q3 occurrence", "consequence": "A current correction is misrepresented as historical operation. The selected action “Run the review now and label it as the missing Q3 occurrence” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at coverage_check.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "Running the activity now may correct the present state, but it cannot recreate evidence that Q3 occurred.", "next_stage": "refresh_action", "risk_outcome": "control_failure", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -12, "evidence": -12, "escalation": -12, "remediation": -12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.33", "a.5.35"], "display_order": 3, "authored_risk_outcome": "evidence_compromised", "remediation": "Reperform assess occurrence coverage using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "remove_q3_from_sample", "label": "Exclude Q3 from the sample and present only the quarters with records", "consequence": "The sample is shaped to hide the known gap. The selected action “Exclude Q3 from the sample and present only the quarters with records” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at coverage_check.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "Known missing coverage must be disclosed; selectively removing it undermines independent review.", "next_stage": "refresh_action", "risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -8, "evidence": -8, "escalation": -8, "remediation": -8}, "control_refs": ["a.5.35"], "display_order": 4, "authored_risk_outcome": "audit_integrity_risk", "remediation": "Reperform assess occurrence coverage using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}], "objective_id": "objective_2", "objective": "Count recurring evidence by expected occurrence across the audit period", "evidence_task": {"prompt": "Assess occurrence coverage", "required_attributes": ["source", "owner", "operating_period", "authenticity", "completeness"]}}, {"id": "refresh_action", "sequence": 3, "agent_message": "The Q4 review did happen and the identity platform still holds the signed export. Our folder copy is undated. What should the evidence owner do before fieldwork?", "demands": ["Choose a truthful refresh action", "Preserve the original record"], "terminal": false, "choices": [{"id": "repull_source_record", "label": "Re-pull the signed export with its internal date visible and retain source provenance", "consequence": "The owner obtains an attributable copy without changing the historical record. The selected action “Re-pull the signed export with its internal date visible and retain source provenance” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at refresh_action.", "is_correct": true, "rationale": "Re-exporting an existing source record preserves what occurred while making its date and origin visible.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "controlled", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 12, "evidence": 12, "escalation": 12, "remediation": 12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.33"], "display_order": 1, "authored_risk_outcome": "controlled", "remediation": "Reperform choose a truthful refresh action using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "edit_existing_copy", "label": "Add the expected date to the undated folder copy", "consequence": "The evidence is altered rather than recovered from its authoritative source. The selected action “Add the expected date to the undated folder copy” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at refresh_action.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "Dates must come from the record itself or its authoritative source; editing the copy weakens integrity.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 5, "evidence": 5, "escalation": 6, "remediation": -2}, "control_refs": ["a.5.33"], "display_order": 2, "authored_risk_outcome": "evidence_compromised", "remediation": "Reperform choose a truthful refresh action using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "use_current_state", "label": "Take a current screenshot and use it as proof that Q4 happened", "consequence": "Current configuration is substituted for evidence of the historical review. The selected action “Take a current screenshot and use it as proof that Q4 happened” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at refresh_action.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "A current screenshot proves current state only; it does not prove that the Q4 review occurred.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "control_failure", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -12, "evidence": -12, "escalation": -12, "remediation": -12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.33"], "display_order": 3, "authored_risk_outcome": "unsupported_claim", "remediation": "Reperform choose a truthful refresh action using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "leave_undated", "label": "Submit the undated copy with an explanatory note from the owner", "consequence": "The explanation does not repair the missing date or source attribution. The selected action “Submit the undated copy with an explanatory note from the owner” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at refresh_action.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "An owner note may explain the gap but does not transform an undated copy into dated evidence.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -8, "evidence": -8, "escalation": -8, "remediation": -8}, "control_refs": ["a.5.33"], "display_order": 4, "authored_risk_outcome": "evidence_stale", "remediation": "Reperform choose a truthful refresh action using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}], "objective_id": "objective_3", "objective": "Choose an honest refresh action without recreating historical evidence", "evidence_task": {"prompt": "Choose a truthful refresh action", "required_attributes": ["source", "owner", "operating_period", "authenticity", "completeness"]}}, {"id": "complete", "sequence": 4, "agent_message": "", "demands": [], "terminal": true, "choices": []}], "source_version": "2", "quality": {"standard_version": "practice-quality-v1", "objectives_assessed": ["Use the date inside an artefact rather than its file modification date", "Count recurring evidence by expected occurrence across the audit period", "Choose an honest refresh action without recreating historical evidence"], "target_dimensions": ["control_mapping", "evidence", "escalation", "remediation"], "reviewed_by": "Astra Curriculum Review Board", "reviewed_at": "2026-10-25T14:00:00Z"}, "content_hash": "b059d2a5d0ac1a03053307b4d35c518932057bc4889e391d794fecd3d9bcb2fa"}, {"practice_id": "incident-severity-triage", "slug": "incident_severity_triage", "title": "Incident severity triage", "brief": "Classify a live incident by impact, preserve evidence, start applicable clocks, and escalate proportionately.", "track": "launch-curriculum", "frameworks": ["iso27001", "nis2", "dora"], "difficulty": "practitioner", "entry_stage_id": "impact_assessment", "stages": [{"id": "impact_assessment", "sequence": 1, "agent_message": "Customer authentication is failing in two regions, but alert volume is modest. Operations asks whether this is only a low-severity technical event.", "demands": ["Classify the initial severity from known impact", "Explain the evidence and escalation basis for the decision"], "terminal": false, "choices": [{"id": "impact_assessment_correct", "label": "Declare a provisional high-severity incident, record impact and assumptions, and appoint an incident lead", "consequence": "The decision remains evidenced, bounded, and owned. The selected action “Declare a provisional high-severity incident, record impact and assumptions, and appoint an incident lead” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at impact_assessment.", "is_correct": true, "rationale": "This is the supported response: it preserves accountable evidence and applies a.5.24, a.5.25 proportionately.", "next_stage": "clock_and_evidence", "risk_outcome": "controlled", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 12, "evidence": 12, "escalation": 12, "remediation": 12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.24", "a.5.25"], "display_order": 1, "authored_risk_outcome": "controlled", "remediation": "Reperform classify the initial severity from known impact using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "impact_assessment_qualified", "label": "Open a medium-severity incident while explicitly setting a 15-minute impact reassessment trigger", "consequence": "Immediate exposure is limited, but a time-bound condition remains open. The selected action “Open a medium-severity incident while explicitly setting a 15-minute impact reassessment trigger” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at impact_assessment.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This is a qualified alternative, not the reference answer: it limits immediate exposure but leaves a named evidence or governance condition unresolved under a.5.24, a.5.25.", "next_stage": "clock_and_evidence", "risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 5, "evidence": 5, "escalation": 6, "remediation": -2}, "control_refs": ["a.5.24", "a.5.25"], "display_order": 2, "authored_risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "remediation": "Reperform classify the initial severity from known impact using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "impact_assessment_failure", "label": "Classify it low because only a few alerts fired", "consequence": "The control conclusion is unsupported and risk increases. The selected action “Classify it low because only a few alerts fired” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at impact_assessment.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This fails the control objective because it substitutes an unsupported conclusion for evidence required by a.5.24, a.5.25.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "control_failure", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -12, "evidence": -12, "escalation": -12, "remediation": -12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.24", "a.5.25"], "display_order": 3, "authored_risk_outcome": "control_failure", "remediation": "Reperform classify the initial severity from known impact using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "impact_assessment_defer", "label": "Wait for a complete root cause before opening an incident", "consequence": "The decision clock continues without accountable action. The selected action “Wait for a complete root cause before opening an incident” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at impact_assessment.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "Deferral leaves the risk unmanaged and misses the required escalation or remediation under a.5.24, a.5.25.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -8, "evidence": -8, "escalation": -8, "remediation": -8}, "control_refs": ["a.5.24", "a.5.25"], "display_order": 4, "authored_risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "remediation": "Reperform classify the initial severity from known impact using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}], "objective_id": "objective_1", "objective": "Anchor severity in business impact", "evidence_task": {"prompt": "Classify the initial severity from known impact", "required_attributes": ["source", "owner", "operating_period", "authenticity", "completeness"]}}, {"id": "clock_and_evidence", "sequence": 2, "agent_message": "The team can restore service quickly, but the exact detection and business-awareness times differ across logs and chat.", "demands": ["Protect the timeline and applicable reporting clocks", "Explain the evidence and escalation basis for the decision"], "terminal": false, "choices": [{"id": "clock_and_evidence_correct", "label": "Record both timestamps with sources, preserve logs, and ask legal to determine which clock applies", "consequence": "The decision remains evidenced, bounded, and owned. The selected action “Record both timestamps with sources, preserve logs, and ask legal to determine which clock applies” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at clock_and_evidence.", "is_correct": true, "rationale": "This is the supported response: it preserves accountable evidence and applies a.5.25, a.5.28 proportionately.", "next_stage": "severity_reassessment", "risk_outcome": "controlled", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 12, "evidence": 12, "escalation": 12, "remediation": 12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.25", "a.5.28"], "display_order": 1, "authored_risk_outcome": "controlled", "remediation": "Reperform protect the timeline and applicable reporting clocks using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "clock_and_evidence_qualified", "label": "Record the earliest supportable timestamp and flag the unresolved awareness time for immediate review", "consequence": "Immediate exposure is limited, but a time-bound condition remains open. The selected action “Record the earliest supportable timestamp and flag the unresolved awareness time for immediate review” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at clock_and_evidence.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This is a qualified alternative, not the reference answer: it limits immediate exposure but leaves a named evidence or governance condition unresolved under a.5.25, a.5.28.", "next_stage": "severity_reassessment", "risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 5, "evidence": 5, "escalation": 6, "remediation": -2}, "control_refs": ["a.5.25", "a.5.28"], "display_order": 2, "authored_risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "remediation": "Reperform protect the timeline and applicable reporting clocks using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "clock_and_evidence_failure", "label": "Use the later timestamp to maximize the reporting window", "consequence": "The control conclusion is unsupported and risk increases. The selected action “Use the later timestamp to maximize the reporting window” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at clock_and_evidence.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This fails the control objective because it substitutes an unsupported conclusion for evidence required by a.5.25, a.5.28.", "next_stage": "severity_reassessment", "risk_outcome": "control_failure", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -12, "evidence": -12, "escalation": -12, "remediation": -12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.25", "a.5.28"], "display_order": 3, "authored_risk_outcome": "control_failure", "remediation": "Reperform protect the timeline and applicable reporting clocks using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "clock_and_evidence_defer", "label": "Restore first and reconstruct timestamps from memory tomorrow", "consequence": "The decision clock continues without accountable action. The selected action “Restore first and reconstruct timestamps from memory tomorrow” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at clock_and_evidence.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "Deferral leaves the risk unmanaged and misses the required escalation or remediation under a.5.25, a.5.28.", "next_stage": "severity_reassessment", "risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -8, "evidence": -8, "escalation": -8, "remediation": -8}, "control_refs": ["a.5.25", "a.5.28"], "display_order": 4, "authored_risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "remediation": "Reperform protect the timeline and applicable reporting clocks using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}], "objective_id": "objective_2", "objective": "Preserve detection and awareness times", "evidence_task": {"prompt": "Protect the timeline and applicable reporting clocks", "required_attributes": ["source", "owner", "operating_period", "authenticity", "completeness"]}}, {"id": "severity_reassessment", "sequence": 3, "agent_message": "Service is restored, but 18,000 customers were unable to authenticate and regulated transactions were delayed.", "demands": ["Reassess severity and escalation after containment", "Explain the evidence and escalation basis for the decision"], "terminal": false, "choices": [{"id": "severity_reassessment_correct", "label": "Keep the incident major, escalate regulatory assessment, and document why restoration does not erase impact", "consequence": "The decision remains evidenced, bounded, and owned. The selected action “Keep the incident major, escalate regulatory assessment, and document why restoration does not erase impact” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at severity_reassessment.", "is_correct": true, "rationale": "This is the supported response: it preserves accountable evidence and applies a.5.26, a.5.27 proportionately.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "controlled", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 12, "evidence": 12, "escalation": 12, "remediation": 12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.26", "a.5.27"], "display_order": 1, "authored_risk_outcome": "controlled", "remediation": "Reperform reassess severity and escalation after containment using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "severity_reassessment_qualified", "label": "Downgrade only operational urgency while retaining major-incident reporting and evidence duties", "consequence": "Immediate exposure is limited, but a time-bound condition remains open. The selected action “Downgrade only operational urgency while retaining major-incident reporting and evidence duties” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at severity_reassessment.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This is a qualified alternative, not the reference answer: it limits immediate exposure but leaves a named evidence or governance condition unresolved under a.5.26, a.5.27.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 5, "evidence": 5, "escalation": 6, "remediation": -2}, "control_refs": ["a.5.26", "a.5.27"], "display_order": 2, "authored_risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "remediation": "Reperform reassess severity and escalation after containment using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "severity_reassessment_failure", "label": "Close as minor because service is now restored", "consequence": "The control conclusion is unsupported and risk increases. The selected action “Close as minor because service is now restored” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at severity_reassessment.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This fails the control objective because it substitutes an unsupported conclusion for evidence required by a.5.26, a.5.27.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "control_failure", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -12, "evidence": -12, "escalation": -12, "remediation": -12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.26", "a.5.27"], "display_order": 3, "authored_risk_outcome": "control_failure", "remediation": "Reperform reassess severity and escalation after containment using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "severity_reassessment_defer", "label": "Leave severity unchanged without documenting the new facts", "consequence": "The decision clock continues without accountable action. The selected action “Leave severity unchanged without documenting the new facts” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at severity_reassessment.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "Deferral leaves the risk unmanaged and misses the required escalation or remediation under a.5.26, a.5.27.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -8, "evidence": -8, "escalation": -8, "remediation": -8}, "control_refs": ["a.5.26", "a.5.27"], "display_order": 4, "authored_risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "remediation": "Reperform reassess severity and escalation after containment using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}], "objective_id": "objective_3", "objective": "Escalate against defined thresholds", "evidence_task": {"prompt": "Reassess severity and escalation after containment", "required_attributes": ["source", "owner", "operating_period", "authenticity", "completeness"]}}, {"id": "complete", "sequence": 4, "agent_message": "", "demands": [], "terminal": true, "choices": []}], "source_version": "1", "quality": {"standard_version": "practice-quality-v1", "objectives_assessed": ["Anchor severity in business impact", "Preserve detection and awareness times", "Escalate against defined thresholds"], "target_dimensions": ["control_mapping", "evidence", "escalation", "remediation"], "reviewed_by": "Astra Curriculum Review Board", "reviewed_at": "2026-10-25T14:00:00Z"}, "content_hash": "4260a82c8753e8fb387384e926f894dd1c2bf9a62123b0c2be6f1631883a4df5"}, {"practice_id": "nonconformity-root-cause-and-corrective-action", "slug": "nonconformity_correc