 "remediation": "Reperform identify a controllable root cause using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "root_cause_qualified", "label": "Record training weakness as a contributing cause while continuing analysis of feed and monitoring design", "consequence": "Immediate exposure is limited, but a time-bound condition remains open. The selected action “Record training weakness as a contributing cause while continuing analysis of feed and monitoring design” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at root_cause.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This is a qualified alternative, not the reference answer: it limits immediate exposure but leaves a named evidence or governance condition unresolved under clause.10.2, a.5.18.", "next_stage": "effectiveness", "risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 5, "evidence": 5, "escalation": 6, "remediation": -2}, "control_refs": ["clause.10.2", "a.5.18"], "display_order": 2, "authored_risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "remediation": "Reperform identify a controllable root cause using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "root_cause_failure", "label": "Name the analyst who missed the tickets as the root cause", "consequence": "The control conclusion is unsupported and risk increases. The selected action “Name the analyst who missed the tickets as the root cause” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at root_cause.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This fails the control objective because it substitutes an unsupported conclusion for evidence required by clause.10.2, a.5.18.", "next_stage": "effectiveness", "risk_outcome": "control_failure", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -12, "evidence": -12, "escalation": -12, "remediation": -12}, "control_refs": ["clause.10.2", "a.5.18"], "display_order": 3, "authored_risk_outcome": "control_failure", "remediation": "Reperform identify a controllable root cause using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "root_cause_defer", "label": "Choose the quickest plausible cause without testing it", "consequence": "The decision clock continues without accountable action. The selected action “Choose the quickest plausible cause without testing it” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at root_cause.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "Deferral leaves the risk unmanaged and misses the required escalation or remediation under clause.10.2, a.5.18.", "next_stage": "effectiveness", "risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -8, "evidence": -8, "escalation": -8, "remediation": -8}, "control_refs": ["clause.10.2", "a.5.18"], "display_order": 4, "authored_risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "remediation": "Reperform identify a controllable root cause using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}], "objective_id": "objective_2", "objective": "Trace causes to controlled processes", "evidence_task": {"prompt": "Identify a controllable root cause", "required_attributes": ["source", "owner", "operating_period", "authenticity", "completeness"]}}, {"id": "effectiveness", "sequence": 3, "agent_message": "A workflow fix is ready. The owner proposes checking the original six accounts next week as proof of effectiveness.", "demands": ["Design the extent and effectiveness checks", "Explain the evidence and escalation basis for the decision"], "terminal": false, "choices": [{"id": "effectiveness_correct", "label": "Test all termination feeds, sample new leavers over two cycles, and define zero unexplained active accounts as the criterion", "consequence": "The decision remains evidenced, bounded, and owned. The selected action “Test all termination feeds, sample new leavers over two cycles, and define zero unexplained active accounts as the criterion” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at effectiveness.", "is_correct": true, "rationale": "This is the supported response: it preserves accountable evidence and applies clause.10.2, a.5.35 proportionately.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "controlled", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 12, "evidence": 12, "escalation": 12, "remediation": 12}, "control_refs": ["clause.10.2", "a.5.35"], "display_order": 1, "authored_risk_outcome": "controlled", "remediation": "Reperform design the extent and effectiveness checks using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "effectiveness_qualified", "label": "Test all feeds once now and schedule a second-cycle review before closure", "consequence": "Immediate exposure is limited, but a time-bound condition remains open. The selected action “Test all feeds once now and schedule a second-cycle review before closure” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at effectiveness.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This is a qualified alternative, not the reference answer: it limits immediate exposure but leaves a named evidence or governance condition unresolved under clause.10.2, a.5.35.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 5, "evidence": 5, "escalation": 6, "remediation": -2}, "control_refs": ["clause.10.2", "a.5.35"], "display_order": 2, "authored_risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "remediation": "Reperform design the extent and effectiveness checks using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "effectiveness_failure", "label": "Retest only the six corrected accounts", "consequence": "The control conclusion is unsupported and risk increases. The selected action “Retest only the six corrected accounts” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at effectiveness.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This fails the control objective because it substitutes an unsupported conclusion for evidence required by clause.10.2, a.5.35.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "control_failure", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -12, "evidence": -12, "escalation": -12, "remediation": -12}, "control_refs": ["clause.10.2", "a.5.35"], "display_order": 3, "authored_risk_outcome": "control_failure", "remediation": "Reperform design the extent and effectiveness checks using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "effectiveness_defer", "label": "Close when the code deploys without measuring outcomes", "consequence": "The decision clock continues without accountable action. The selected action “Close when the code deploys without measuring outcomes” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at effectiveness.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "Deferral leaves the risk unmanaged and misses the required escalation or remediation under clause.10.2, a.5.35.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -8, "evidence": -8, "escalation": -8, "remediation": -8}, "control_refs": ["clause.10.2", "a.5.35"], "display_order": 4, "authored_risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "remediation": "Reperform design the extent and effectiveness checks using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}], "objective_id": "objective_3", "objective": "Define an extent check and effectiveness test", "evidence_task": {"prompt": "Design the extent and effectiveness checks", "required_attributes": ["source", "owner", "operating_period", "authenticity", "completeness"]}}, {"id": "complete", "sequence": 4, "agent_message": "", "demands": [], "terminal": true, "choices": []}], "source_version": "1", "quality": {"standard_version": "practice-quality-v1", "objectives_assessed": ["Separate containment from systemic correction", "Trace causes to controlled processes", "Define an extent check and effectiveness test"], "target_dimensions": ["control_mapping", "evidence", "escalation", "remediation"], "reviewed_by": "Astra Curriculum Review Board", "reviewed_at": "2026-10-25T14:00:00Z"}, "content_hash": "e3b959cfb8a7ce91d65b0dd2cc6f263640e2556f65bdd32ca73cccfc6df0f63f"}, {"practice_id": "ransomware-group-response", "slug": "ransomware_group_response", "title": "Ransomware: Group-Wide Business Continuity Invocation", "brief": "You are the Group CISO of a multi-entity international group operating across six entities in six jurisdictions. At 06:15 on a Monday, your SOC alerts you that ransomware has encrypted the file servers of your largest subsidiary. The subsidiary accounts for 40% of group revenue. Three other entities share network segments with the affected subsidiary. Backups exist but have not been tested in nine months. Your board convenes in four hours. Your decisions determine invocation, containment, communication, and recovery sequencing across the group.", "track": "ai-risk-lead", "frameworks": ["iso27001-2022"], "difficulty": "expert", "entry_stage_id": "invocation_decision", "stages": [{"id": "invocation_decision", "sequence": 1, "agent_message": "SOC confirms ransomware on the subsidiary file servers. Encryption is still running — it started approximately 90 minutes ago. Three shared network segments connect to other entities. We have not isolated yet because isolation takes down the shared ERP system that all six entities depend on for daily operations. The ransom note is on screen. What is your call?", "demands": ["Whether to invoke business continuity now", "Whether to isolate the subsidiary immediately", "Whether to engage law enforcement", "Who owns the decision if you are unavailable"], "terminal": false, "choices": [{"id": "invoke_and_isolate", "label": "Invoke BCP and isolate the subsidiary now", "consequence": "Business continuity is invoked across the group. The subsidiary is isolated immediately, taking down the shared ERP. All six entities lose ERP access but the spread vector is closed. The incident timeline is clean from invocation. The selected action “Invoke BCP and isolate the subsidiary now” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at invocation_decision.", "is_correct": true, "rationale": "Satisfies ISO 27001:2022 A.5.29 (information security during disruption) and A.5.30 (ICT readiness for business continuity). Isolation is the correct containment action under A.5.26 even at operational cost — the spread risk to three connected entities outweighs the ERP disruption. BCP invocation ensures the response is governed and auditable.", "next_stage": "containment_strategy", "risk_outcome": "controlled", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 12, "evidence": 12, "escalation": 12, "remediation": 12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.29", "a.5.30", "a.5.26"], "display_order": 1, "authored_risk_outcome": "controlled", "remediation": "Reperform whether to invoke business continuity now using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "contain_without_bcp", "label": "Contain technically — do not invoke BCP yet", "consequence": "IT attempts technical containment without formal BCP invocation. The response is ungoverned, decision authority is unclear, and the board has no formal briefing obligation. Containment may succeed but the response has no auditable governance structure. The selected action “Contain technically — do not invoke BCP yet” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at invocation_decision.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "Fails ISO 27001:2022 A.5.29 — BCP exists to govern the response to disruption, not only to restore services. Containing without invocation means no defined roles, no escalation path, and no recovery time objective in force. The three connected entities remain at unquantified risk without a formal response framework.", "next_stage": "containment_strategy", "risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 5, "evidence": 5, "escalation": 6, "remediation": -2}, "control_refs": ["a.5.29"], "display_order": 2, "authored_risk_outcome": "ungoverned", "remediation": "Reperform whether to invoke business continuity now using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "pay_ransom_first", "label": "Negotiate the ransom — explore payment before isolation", "consequence": "Ransom negotiation begins while encryption continues. The spread window stays open across the three connected entities. Payment does not guarantee decryption and may violate sanctions obligations depending on the threat actor's jurisdiction. The selected action “Negotiate the ransom — explore payment before isolation” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at invocation_decision.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "Fails ISO 27001:2022 A.5.26 and A.5.29 — the incident response obligation is to contain and recover, not to negotiate while the attack is active. A.8.13 (information backup) and A.5.30 require a recovery path that does not depend on attacker cooperation. Sanctions risk is a legal exposure outside the ISMS but material to the decision.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "control_failure", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -12, "evidence": -12, "escalation": -12, "remediation": -12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.26", "a.5.29", "a.5.30", "a.8.13"], "display_order": 3, "authored_risk_outcome": "spread_risk", "remediation": "Reperform whether to invoke business continuity now using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "wait_for_forensics", "label": "Wait for forensic confirmation before invoking", "consequence": "No BCP invocation until forensics confirm scope. Encryption continues during the forensic window. The three connected entities remain exposed. The board meeting arrives with no formal response structure in place. The selected action “Wait for forensic confirmation before invoking” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at invocation_decision.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "Fails ISO 27001:2022 A.5.29 and A.5.30 — BCP invocation is triggered by disruption to critical operations, not by forensic confirmation of scope. Waiting extends the spread window and leaves the response ungoverned. Forensics run in parallel with containment, not before it.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -8, "evidence": -8, "escalation": -8, "remediation": -8}, "control_refs": ["a.5.29", "a.5.30"], "display_order": 4, "authored_risk_outcome": "spread_risk", "remediation": "Reperform whether to invoke business continuity now using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}], "objective_id": "objective_1", "objective": "Invoke continuity and isolate affected systems", "evidence_task": {"prompt": "Whether to invoke business continuity now", "required_attributes": ["source", "owner", "operating_period", "authenticity", "completeness"]}}, {"id": "containment_strategy", "sequence": 2, "agent_message": "Business continuity is invoked. Subsidiary is isolated — ERP is down for all six entities. IT confirms backups exist for the subsidiary but the last tested restore was nine months ago. Restore time estimate is 18-36 hours, unverified. The three connected entities are clean so far but we cannot confirm lateral movement has not occurred. The ransom demand is 2.1 million euros with a 48-hour deadline. What is your containment position?", "demands": ["Whether to forensically image before restoring", "Whether to scan the three connected entities now", "Your position on the ransom demand", "Backup restoration sequencing across the group"], "terminal": false, "choices": [{"id": "image_then_restore", "label": "Forensic image first — then restore from backup", "consequence": "All affected systems are forensically imaged before restoration begins. Evidence is preserved end to end. Restore begins after imaging with the 28-hour timeline. Connected entities are scanned in parallel. Ransom is declined. The selected action “Forensic image first — then restore from backup” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at containment_strategy.", "is_correct": true, "rationale": "Satisfies ISO 27001:2022 A.5.28 (collection of evidence), A.8.13 (information backup), and A.5.30. Forensic imaging before restoration preserves the evidence chain for law enforcement and insurance. Declining the ransom is consistent with A.5.29 — recovery must not depend on attacker cooperation when a tested backup path exists, and the backup exists even if untested.", "next_stage": "board_communication", "risk_outcome": "controlled", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 12, "evidence": 12, "escalation": 12, "remediation": 12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.28", "a.5.29", "a.5.30", "a.8.13"], "display_order": 1, "authored_risk_outcome": "controlled", "remediation": "Reperform whether to forensically image before restoring using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "restore_immediately", "label": "Restore from backup immediately — speed first", "consequence": "Restoration begins without forensic imaging. Systems are back online faster but the evidence chain is destroyed. Law enforcement cannot prosecute and insurance claims are unsupportable without forensic evidence. The selected action “Restore from backup immediately — speed first” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at containment_strategy.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "Fails ISO 27001:2022 A.5.28 — evidence must be collected before remediation where possible. Restoring without imaging destroys the forensic record. A.5.30 requires ICT recovery to be evidenced and auditable — an unevidenced restore cannot support post-incident review or regulatory inquiry.", "next_stage": "board_communication", "risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 5, "evidence": 5, "escalation": 6, "remediation": -2}, "control_refs": ["a.5.28", "a.5.30"], "display_order": 2, "authored_risk_outcome": "evidence_destroyed", "remediation": "Reperform whether to forensically image before restoring using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "pay_and_decrypt", "label": "Pay the ransom — decrypt rather than restore", "consequence": "Payment is made. Decryption keys are provided and systems are restored faster than the 28-hour backup path. No forensic imaging. Sanctions risk materialises if the threat actor is on a restricted list. The attacker is funded for the next attack. The selected action “Pay the ransom — decrypt rather than restore” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at containment_strategy.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "Fails ISO 27001:2022 A.5.28 and A.5.29. Payment without forensic imaging destroys evidence and funds the threat actor. A.8.13 requires backup capability precisely to avoid operational dependency on attacker cooperation. Sanctions exposure is a material legal risk outside the ISMS that the CISO must escalate to legal before any payment is considered.", "next_stage": "board_communication", "risk_outcome": "control_failure", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -12, "evidence": -12, "escalation": -12, "remediation": -12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.28", "a.5.29", "a.8.13"], "display_order": 3, "authored_risk_outcome": "sanctions_risk", "remediation": "Reperform whether to forensically image before restoring using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "containment_strategy_unmanaged_delay", "label": "Wait for another team before assigning ownership for whether to forensically image before restoring", "consequence": "The decision to “Wait for another team before assigning ownership for whether to forensically image before restoring” changes the evidence trail, accountable owner, and residual risk for this specific containment strategy decision. The selected action “Wait for another team before assigning ownership for whether to forensically image before restoring” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at containment_strategy.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This unmanaged delay response is assessed against a.5.28, a.5.29, a.5.30, a.8.13 and the requirement for attributable evidence, bounded authority, and a dated next action.", "next_stage": "board_communication", "risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -8, "evidence": -8, "escalation": -8, "remediation": -8}, "control_refs": ["a.5.28", "a.5.29", "a.5.30", "a.8.13"], "display_order": 4, "remediation": "Reperform whether to forensically image before restoring using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}], "objective_id": "objective_2", "objective": "Preserve forensic evidence before restoration", "evidence_task": {"prompt": "Whether to forensically image before restoring", "required_attributes": ["source", "owner", "operating_period", "authenticity", "completeness"]}}, {"id": "board_communication", "sequence": 3, "agent_message": "Forensic imaging is underway. Connected entities are being scanned — two are clean, one has suspicious lateral movement indicators but no confirmed encryption. Restore estimate is 28 hours for the subsidiary. The board convenes in 90 minutes. General counsel wants to know your notification position across the six jurisdictions before the board meeting — GDPR, NIS2, and local breach notification laws apply differently across the group. What do you tell the board and what do you notify externally?", "demands": ["Board communication scope and framing", "Supervisory authority notification position", "NIS2 early warning decision (where applicable)", "Whether affected customers are notified now"], "terminal": false, "choices": [{"id": "full_disclosure_notify_all", "label": "Full board disclosure — notify all authorities across all jurisdictions now", "consequence": "The board receives a complete incident briefing. Supervisory authority notifications are filed across all six jurisdictions simultaneously. NIS2 early warning is filed where applicable. Customer notification is issued group-wide. The selected action “Full board disclosure — notify all authorities across all jurisdictions now” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at board_communication.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "ISO 27001:2022 A.5.26 requires notification through proper channels with accurate scope. Filing across all jurisdictions simultaneously before scope is confirmed in the three connected entities risks materially inaccurate notifications. GDPR Article 33 and NIS2 obligations are jurisdiction-specific — a blanket filing without confirmed scope in each entity is procedurally premature and may require amendment.", "next_stage": "synthesis_4", "risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 5, "evidence": 5, "escalation": 6, "remediation": -2}, "control_refs": ["a.5.26"], "display_order": 1, "authored_risk_outcome": "premature_notification", "remediation": "Reperform board communication scope and framing using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "board_brief_staged_notify", "label": "Board briefing with staged notification — confirmed entities first", "consequence": "The board receives a full briefing on confirmed scope and ongoing investigation. Authority notifications are filed for the confirmed subsidiary only. NIS2 early warning is filed where the subsidiary operates. Connected entity notifications are staged pending scan confirmation. Customer notification follows scope confirmation. The selected action “Board briefing with staged notification — confirmed entities first” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at board_communication.", "is_correct": true, "rationale": "Satisfies ISO 27001:2022 A.5.26 and A.5.29. Staged notification matches confirmed scope to each jurisdiction's obligation — GDPR Article 33 for the subsidiary's data subjects, NIS2 early warning where applicable, with connected entity notifications triggered by scan results. Board briefing ensures governance is visible at the right level without overstating scope.", "next_stage": "synthesis_4", "risk_outcome": "controlled", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 12, "evidence": 12, "escalation": 12, "remediation": 12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.26", "a.5.29"], "display_order": 2, "authored_risk_outcome": "controlled", "remediation": "Reperform board communication scope and framing using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "defer_all_notification", "label": "Defer all external notification — brief board only, notify when fully resolved", "consequence": "The board is briefed but no external notifications are filed. Notification is deferred until full recovery and scope confirmation. GDPR 72-hour and NIS2 24-hour windows close during the deferral period. The selected action “Defer all external notification — brief board only, notify when fully resolved” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at board_communication.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "Fails GDPR Article 33 and NIS2 Article 19 — both impose time-bound notification obligations that run from awareness, not from resolution. ISO 27001:2022 A.5.26 requires timely notification through defined channels. Deferring until resolution guarantees late notification across multiple jurisdictions and compounds the regulatory exposure.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "control_failure", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -12, "evidence": -12, "escalation": -12, "remediation": -12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.26"], "display_order": 3, "authored_risk_outcome": "late_notification", "remediation": "Reperform board communication scope and framing using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "board_communication_unmanaged_delay", "label": "Wait for another team before assigning ownership for board communication scope and framing", "consequence": "The decision to “Wait for another team before assigning ownership for board communication scope and framing” changes the evidence trail, accountable owner, and residual risk for this specific board communication decision. The selected action “Wait for another team before assigning ownership for board communication scope and framing” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at board_communication.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This unmanaged delay response is assessed against a.5.26 and the requirement for attributable evidence, bounded authority, and a dated next action.", "next_stage": "synthesis_4", "risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -8, "evidence": -8, "escalation": -8, "remediation": -8}, "control_refs": ["a.5.26"], "display_order": 4, "remediation": "Reperform board communication scope and framing using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}], "objective_id": "objective_3", "objective": "Stage accurate executive and regulatory communication", "evidence_task": {"prompt": "Board communication scope and framing", "required_attributes": ["source", "owner", "operating_period", "authenticity", "completeness"]}}, {"id": "synthesis_4", "sequence": 4, "agent_message": "Before closure, the reviewer asks for one defensible conclusion that links the decisions in Ransomware: Group-Wide Business Continuity Invocation to retained evidence and residual risk.", "demands": ["Synthesise the evidence and justify closure for stage accurate executive and regulatory communication", "State the limitation that would prevent closure"], "terminal": false, "choices": [{"id": "synthesis_4_controlled", "label": "Document and execute the evidenced response for synthesise the evidence and justify closure for stage accurate executive and regulatory communication", "consequence": "The decision to “Document and execute the evidenced response for synthesise the evidence and justify closure for stage accurate executive and regulatory communication” changes the evidence trail, accountable owner, and residual risk for this specific synthesis 4 decision. The selected action “Document and execute the evidenced response for synthesise the evidence and justify closure for stage accurate executive and regulatory communication” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at synthesis_4.", "is_correct": true, "rationale": "This controlled response is assessed against a.5.26, a.5.28, a.5.29 and the requirement for attributable evidence, bounded authority, and a dated next action.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "controlled", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 12, "evidence": 12, "escalation": 12, "remediation": 12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.26", "a.5.28", "a.5.29"], "display_order": 1, "remediation": "Reperform synthesise the evidence and justify closure for stage accurate executive and regulatory communication using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check.", "authored_risk_outcome": "controlled"}, {"id": "synthesis_4_qualified_alternative", "label": "Contain the immediate issue and time-box the remaining work for synthesise the evidence and justify closure for stage accurate executive and regulatory communication", "consequence": "The decision to “Contain the immediate issue and time-box the remaining work for synthesise the evidence and justify closure for stage accurate executive and regulatory communication” changes the evidence trail, accountable owner, and residual risk for this specific synthesis 4 decision. The selected action “Contain the immediate issue and time-box the remaining work for synthesise the evidence and justify closure for stage accurate executive and regulatory communication” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at synthesis_4.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This qualified alternative response is assessed against a.5.26, a.5.28, a.5.29 and the requirement for attributable evidence, bounded authority, and a dated next action.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 5, "evidence": 5, "escalation": 6, "remediation": -2}, "control_refs": ["a.5.26", "a.5.28", "a.5.29"], "display_order": 2, "remediation": "Reperform synthesise the evidence and justify closure for stage accurate executive and regulatory communication using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check.", "authored_risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative"}, {"id": "synthesis_4_control_failure", "label": "Accept the current position without independently testing synthesise the evidence and justify closure for stage accurate executive and regulatory communication", "consequence": "The decision to “Accept the current position without independently testing synthesise the evidence and justify closure for stage accurate executive and regulatory communication” changes the evidence trail, accountable owner, and residual risk for this specific synthesis 4 decision. The selected action “Accept the current position without independently testing synthesise the evidence and justify closure for stage accurate executive and regulatory communication” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at synthesis_4.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This control failure response is assessed against a.5.26, a.5.28, a.5.29 and the requirement for attributable evidence, bounded authority, and a dated next action.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "control_failure", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -12, "evidence": -12, "escalation": -12, "remediation": -12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.26", "a.5.28", "a.5.29"], "display_order": 3, "remediation": "Reperform synthesise the evidence and justify closure for stage accurate executive and regulatory communication using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check.", "authored_risk_outcome": "control_failure"}, {"id": "synthesis_4_unmanaged_delay", "label": "Wait for another team before assigning ownership for synthesise the evidence and justify closure for stage accurate executive and regulatory communication", "consequence": "The decision to “Wait for another team before assigning ownership for synthesise the evidence and justify closure for stage accurate executive and regulatory communication” changes the evidence trail, accountable owner, and residual risk for this specific synthesis 4 decision. The selected action “Wait for another team before assigning ownership for synthesise the evidence and justify closure for stage accurate executive and regulatory communication” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at synthesis_4.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This unmanaged delay response is assessed against a.5.26, a.5.28, a.5.29 and the requirement for attributable evidence, bounded authority, and a dated next action.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -8, "evidence": -8, "escalation": -8, "remediation": -8}, "control_refs": ["a.5.26", "a.5.28", "a.5.29"], "display_order": 4, "remediation": "Reperform synthesise the evidence and justify closure for stage accurate executive and regulatory communication using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check.", "authored_risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay"}], "objective_id": "objective_3", "objective": "Stage accurate executive and regulatory communication", "evidence_task": {"prompt": "Synthesise the evidence and justify closure for stage accurate executive and regulatory communication", "required_attributes": ["source", "owner", "operating_period", "authenticity", "completeness"]}}, {"id": "complete", "sequence": 5, "agent_message": "Understood. Your response position across all four decision points is recorded. The group will operate within the scope you have defined. Recovery sequencing and external notifications will proceed accordingly.", "demands": [], "terminal": true, "choices": []}], "source_version": "2", "quality": {"standard_version": "practice-quality-v1", "objectives_assessed": ["Invoke continuity and isolate affected systems", "Preserve forensic evidence before restoration", "Stage accurate executive and regulatory communication"], "target_dimensions": ["control_mapping", "evidence", "escalation", "remediation"], "reviewed_by": "Astra Curriculum Review Board", "reviewed_at": "2026-10-25T14:00:00Z"}, "content_hash": "53026ccdbdf18906c08982426a41b28e2037bf86af9351a52ade1b9fdb166212"}, {"practice_id": "risk-acceptance-memo", "slug": "risk_acceptance_memo", "title": "Risk acceptance memo", "brief": "Test whether acceptance is justified and identify authority, conditions, expiry, and reopen triggers.", "track": "launch-curriculum", "frameworks": ["iso27001", "dora"], "difficulty": "expert", "entry_stage_id": "decision_basis", "stages": [{"id": "decision_basis", "sequence": 1, "agent_message": "A legacy payment service cannot support MFA for administrators. The product team asks to accept the risk until replacement next year.", "demands": ["Test whether the acceptance basis is complete", "Explain the evidence and escalation basis for the decision"], "terminal": false, "choices": [{"id": "decision_basis_correct", "label": "Document threat, exposure, residual likelihood and impact, alternatives, and current compensating controls", "consequence": "The decision remains evidenced, bounded, and owned. The selected action “Document threat, exposure, residual likelihood and impact, alternatives, and current compensating controls” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at decision_basis.", "is_correct": true, "rationale": "This is the supported response: it preserves accountable evidence and applies a.5.7, a.5.15 proportionately.", "next_stage": "authority", "risk_outcome": "controlled", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 12, "evidence": 12, "escalation": 12, "remediation": 12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.7", "a.5.15"], "display_order": 1, "authored_risk_outcome": "controlled", "remediation": "Reperform test whether the acceptance basis is complete using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "decision_basis_qualified", "label": "Draft a provisional memo using current facts but mark missing threat evidence as a blocker to final approval", "consequence": "Immediate exposure is limited, but a time-bound condition remains open. The selected action “Draft a provisional memo using current facts but mark missing threat evidence as a blocker to final approval” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at decision_basis.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This is a qualified alternative, not the reference answer: it limits immediate exposure but leaves a named evidence or governance condition unresolved under a.5.7, a.5.15.", "next_stage": "authority", "risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 5, "evidence": 5, "escalation": 6, "remediation": -2}, "control_refs": ["a.5.7", "a.5.15"], "display_order": 2, "authored_risk_outcome": "qualified_alternative", "remediation": "Reperform test whether the acceptance basis is complete using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "decision_basis_failure", "label": "State that replacement cost alone justifies acceptance", "consequence": "The control conclusion is unsupported and risk increases. The selected action “State that replacement cost alone justifies acceptance” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at decision_basis.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This fails the control objective because it substitutes an unsupported conclusion for evidence required by a.5.7, a.5.15.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "control_failure", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -12, "evidence": -12, "escalation": -12, "remediation": -12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.7", "a.5.15"], "display_order": 3, "authored_risk_outcome": "control_failure", "remediation": "Reperform test whether the acceptance basis is complete using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "decision_basis_defer", "label": "Copy last year's acceptance without reassessment", "consequence": "The decision clock continues without accountable action. The selected action “Copy last year's acceptance without reassessment” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at decision_basis.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "Deferral leaves the risk unmanaged and misses the required escalation or remediation under a.5.7, a.5.15.", "next_stage": "complete", "risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -8, "evidence": -8, "escalation": -8, "remediation": -8}, "control_refs": ["a.5.7", "a.5.15"], "display_order": 4, "authored_risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "remediation": "Reperform test whether the acceptance basis is complete using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}], "objective_id": "objective_1", "objective": "Recognize treatment deferral disguised as acceptance", "evidence_task": {"prompt": "Test whether the acceptance basis is complete", "required_attributes": ["source", "owner", "operating_period", "authenticity", "completeness"]}}, {"id": "authority", "sequence": 2, "agent_message": "The product director offers to sign today, although the risk method assigns critical residual risks to the executive committee.", "demands": ["Route the decision to valid authority", "Explain the evidence and escalation basis for the decision"], "terminal": false, "choices": [{"id": "authority_correct", "label": "Send the evidenced recommendation to the executive committee and record the product director as accountable owner, not approver", "consequence": "The decision remains evidenced, bounded, and owned. The selected action “Send the evidenced recommendation to the executive committee and record the product director as accountable owner, not approver” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at authority.", "is_correct": true, "rationale": "This is the supported response: it preserves accountable evidence and applies a.5.1, a.5.2 proportionately.", "next_stage": "conditions", "risk_outcome": "controlled", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 12, "evidence": 12, "escalation": 12, "remediation": 12}, "control_refs": ["a.5.1", "a.5.2"], "display_order": 1, "authored_risk_outcome": "controlled", "remediation": "Reperform route the decision to valid authority using a named owner, attributable evidence, a decision deadline, and an effectiveness check."}, {"id": "authority_qualified", "label": "Obtain interim written sponsorship from the director while prohibiting production expansion pending committee approval", "consequence": "Immediate exposure is limited, but a time-bound condition remains open. The selected action “Obtain interim written sponsorship from the director while prohibiting production expansion pending committee approval” changes ownership, retained evidence, and residual risk at authority.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This is a qualified alternativ